{"slug": "e1-euler-anchor-heat-certificate", "round": 1, "kind": "explore", "verdict": "OBSTRUCTION: The decisive test 2 pi^2 c > C fails for every fixed c > 0: the Euler product modulates the compression ratio q of adjacent zero pairs at the anchor by order 1/L^2 with both signs, above the trace x^{-C/(2 pi^2)} a past collision leaves.", "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "aboutZeros": false, "file": "push/e1-euler-anchor-heat-certificate/RESULT.md", "nodes": ["euler-anchor-heat-certificate", "heat-evolved-von-mangoldt-positivity"], "tags": ["heat-flow", "euler-anchor", "collision", "returns-input"], "obstructionKind": "returns-its-input (region right of 1 does not pass to the line)", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 0, "batch": "engine batch 1", "refereeFile": "push/e1-euler-anchor-heat-certificate/REFEREE.md", "refereeNote": "Lemmas 1, 2 confirmed; Lemma 3 midpoint formula is not the leading order (deficit follows the variation of the log-derivative of the truncated Dirichlet polynomial across the pair, correlation 0.93 to 0.996).", "controlsThatDefeat": ["E_a = zeta(s+a)zeta(s-a): passes the anchor step; constant-S certificate certifies 4 of 12 collided pairs at a = 0.1, L = 6 (unsound without the transport claim)", "lower bound on the deficit does not depend on positivity of the coefficients, so sign twists are not separated"], "addedBy": "c2-repair-owed-passes"}
{"slug": "e1-forcing-free-bilinear-split", "round": 1, "kind": "explore", "verdict": "OBSTRUCTION: After the forcing is removed by two linear conditions on the mollifier, every identity of this shape is a linear combination of the half-weight Legendre identity (1*Lambda = log) with symbol exactly 1 at every zero; at full level Lambda >= 0 is implied (system has the single solution Lambda), and the remaining one-sided polylog bound on K'[R] is equivalent to RH (Theorem OS).", "refereeHolds": false, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "aboutZeros": false, "file": "push/e1-forcing-free-bilinear-split/RESULT.md", "nodes": ["vaughan-sqrt-type1-exact", "vaughan-forcing-law", "landau-one-sided-target"], "tags": ["vaughan", "bilinear", "landau", "legendre-lp", "restatement"], "obstructionKind": "restatement-of-rh", "restatement": true, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 1, "lemmasDecided": 0, "batch": "engine batch 1", "refereeFile": "push/e1-forcing-free-bilinear-split/REFEREE.md", "refereeNote": "Verdict stands. Theorem R(iii) (parity cap at restricted level, labelled PROVED) is false: Theorem P does not apply to Chebyshev-class weights. Also not surviving: uniqueness of the dual certificate, '5-8x', 'X^0.44', '4.7e-7 by proof'.", "controlsThatDefeat": ["E_a = zeta(s+a)zeta(s-a): not excluded by any proved step", "structured sign twist with Lambda >= 0 (TW+): not excluded by any proved step"], "addedBy": "c2-repair-owed-passes"}
