{"round": 16, "slug": "c16-repair-owed-record-r15", "kind": "repair", "verdict": "partial-result", "claim": "Record lane, no attack, nothing about zeros of zeta. Items 1 to 7 entered. Map 202 -> 205 rows (S12b; Q30, since the proposed label Q25 was taken; G41 for DJ and DN with the canonical tier marked NOT CLOSED) plus control rows ZQ, SG, NR-q. 30 label restrictions, E1-E3 in the report, the Lemma L pole clause and the c14 E1 note applied as dated notes. Engine: controls 20 -> 23; device types 50/1/0 -> 53/1/11; pending 8 -> 7. Ten screening lines with referees 0. Statement O version 4 written. Headline 1 of 4 and hold rate 90.8% unchanged; outcomes byte-identical. Top 60 identical after rows and controls; after the eleven silent-cell nodes only 2 of 60 keys remain and 57 stand on those nodes. Missing: REFEREE.md is the author's own pass (42 checks), not independent. Departures: build_graph.py and ENGINE_LOG.md left unedited; nodes-21.json sits outside engine/curated.", "aboutZeros": false, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-repair-owed-record-r15/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": [], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 0, "nodes": [], "tags": ["repair", "record"], "obstructionKind": "record", "owed": "independent referee for this lane (none was available to it); CONTROL_CODE_RE codes NR-q, ZQ, SG; ENGINE_LOG and ROADMAP pointers; device entries for c15-edge and c15-klein; second referee for lines 13 to 17 of Statement O version 4; a decision by the planner on whether the silent-cell nodes stay open devices (57 of the top 60)", "lesson": "Entering read classes as open device nodes is not a neutral record edit. The generator keeps a fixed number of device partners per anchor and weights open devices above the floored one, so eleven new nodes replaced 58 of the top 60 and dropped 13 former candidates from enumeration. Staging the reruns (rows and controls, then nodes, then lane lines) gave each change one cause. Node text that says \"map row X\" makes the builder attach that row and its controls to the node.", "followUp": "Planner decision before using the top 60: keep the eleven silent-cell types as open devices or move them to PENDING (see engine/curated/CHANGELOG_c16-repair.md; the former list is baseline/CANDIDATES.json). Also owed: an independent referee for this lane and a second referee for Statement O v4 lines 13 to 17; the CONTROL_CODE_RE codes NR-q, ZQ, SG; an update of row G41 once c16-dn-canonical-tier-ball-conversion reports.", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta; record lane, no attack. Owed list of round 15 entered: map 202 -> 205 rows (S12b, Q30 for the proposed Q25, G41 for dictionaries DJ and DN with the canonical tier marked NOT CLOSED), control rows ZQ, SG, NR-q with a note on Lemma L and its pole clause; the 30 label restrictions of c15-referee-r14-independent-checkpoint on rows G37 to G41 and the Lemma F note; corrections E1 to E3 in CAMPAIGN_REPORT_R15.md (E3, E4 were already in STRATEGY version 5); pole clause restored in three marked places of the c15 lane-2 RESULT; dated correction note for sentence E1 in the c14 pre-filter RESULT; engine: controls 20 -> 23, device types 50/1/0 -> 53/1/11 with eleven silent-cell nodes (nodes-21.json), pending 8 -> 7; ten lanes.jsonl lines for the screening lanes (referees 0); Statement O version 4 (lines 13 to 17, each on one referee file; section F). Staged control: after rows, controls and closed device types the top 60 is identical in keys, order and scores; after the silent-cell nodes 57 of 60 candidates stand on them (effect of the open-device weight; 13 former candidates no longer enumerated). Headline 1 of 4 and hold rate 90.8% unchanged; lanes run 130 -> 140 (screening lines). outcomes/ and closed_families.json byte-identical; merge_outcomes.py not run. REFEREE.md is the author's mechanical second pass (42 checks), not an independent referee.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "E1 (substantive, engine semantics, only partly disclosed): the eleven silent cells are entered with device state \"open\". In engine/generate.py that state means an open crossing device: it fills the requirement slot \"crossing\", adds weight 2 (line 439) and exempts a candidate from the two -3 penalties for a majority of flow-side or mean-value members (lines 475, 480). The node texts say \"Not a lead\". The live CANDIDATES.json has rank 1 = M3-f0e2d7 (12.03) with crossing = silent-u8, and 57 of 60 w", "surviving": "Record lane; nothing about zeros of zeta. Confirmed on the live files: map 202 -> 205 rows (S12b, Q30, G41 with the canonical tier NOT CLOSED) plus control rows ZQ, SG, NR-q, worded faithfully to the four referee files; 30 label restrictions and the dated notes entered; devices 53 closed / 1 floored / 11 open, pending 7, controls 23; ten screening lines with referees 0; Statement O version 4 written; headline 1 of 4 and hold rate 90.8% unchanged; outcomes byte-identical (142 sha256 values recomputed); top 60 identical after stage 1, 2 of 60 keys left after the silent-cell nodes. Correction: the generator scores the eleven silent cells as open crossing devices (weight 2 and exemption from two penalties), so the current top 60 is an effect of that state and not a ranking of leads; the state should be changed before the list is used. This pass counts as one independent referee; D_+ >= 0 for G_+ now has a second derivation.", "refereeHolds": true}
{"round": 16, "slug": "c16-u6g-scattering-fe-rank2-bridge-stage-a", "kind": "explore", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Cell U6 (g), rank 2: Gram positivity of truncated minimal-parabolic SL3 Eisenstein series (one function M at z1, z2, z1+z2). Proved relative to the recalled inner product formula (Lemma R, checked to 1e-10): the inequality is not closed under Blaschke insertion; a zero with 0 < Re a < 1/2 forces a zero at 1 - a. Symmetric insertions (zeta times a symmetric polynomial, which has f(z) = f(1-z); T-NR is the infinite case) and unpaired zeros right of 1/2 pass at every T >= 0 in about 4,700 Gram matrices of order up to 5 (MEASURED, local; closure not proved). At a hypothetical off-line pair the form at the one computable point is strict, height-independent and positive for every eta, so it gives no contradiction. Lane ends with a device row. Server not used. REFEREE.md is a same-session pass, not independent.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 2, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-u6g-scattering-fe-rank2-bridge-stage-a/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": [], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": true, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 4, "nodes": ["u6g-rank2-eisenstein-gram", "ctrl-bls-symmetric", "ctrl-bls-right", "lemma-r-reflection"], "tags": ["explore", "u6g", "rank2", "eisenstein", "gram-positivity", "control-bls", "stage-a"], "obstructionKind": "control-passes: BLS with a symmetric zero set (polynomial ZQ, T-NR) and BLS with unpaired zeros right of 1/2 pass the rank-2 Gram inequality (measured)", "owed": "independent referee; proof or refutation of closure of the rank-2 form under symmetric and right-unpaired Blaschke factors; source check of the inner product formula and the range of T; wording correction of the BLS control row (Lemma S)", "lesson": "Rank 2 adds one condition to rank one: left-half zeros of the scattering coefficient must be reflected, which is the functional equation of the zero set. Reading f(z) = f(1-z) or the exact normalisation does not leave the Blaschke control: its symmetric form is zeta times a symmetric polynomial and stays positive on a larger set of T than zeta. The BLS control row's \"lacks f(z) = f(1-z)\" is wrong for symmetric zero sets.", "followUp": "Prove or refute closure of the rank-2 Gram form under symmetric and right-unpaired Blaschke factors; cheap first step is a larger adversarial search on the server (order 10 to 20, zero heights to 1e3). Also owed: an independent referee, and a source check of the inner product formula and the valid range of T.", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Cell U6 (g), rank 2. Gram positivity of truncated minimal-parabolic SL3 Eisenstein series (one function M at z1, z2, z1+z2) is not closed under Blaschke insertion: a zero with 0 < Re a < 1/2 forces a zero at 1 - a (Lemma R, proved relative to the recalled inner product formula; checked to 1e-10). Symmetric insertions (zeta times a symmetric polynomial: has f(z) = f(1-z); T-NR is the infinite case) and unpaired zeros with Re a > 1/2 pass at every T >= 0 in about 4,700 Gram matrices of order up to 5 (MEASURED, not proved). At a hypothetical off-line pair the form at the one computable point is strict, independent of the height, and positive for every eta. REFEREE.md is a same-session pass, not independent.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "No PROVED step broke. Lemma R, Lemma S, Lemma D and form (*) were re-derived by hand and confirmed with an independent kernel implementation (no import of gram.py) on new cases: Lemma R defect 3e-11 to 3e-8, also for generic poles p = 0.7 and 2.5; form (*) 1e-20 to 6e-18; M = 1 kite integral 6e-27. Corrections needed before the rows are entered:\n\nE1 (claim too wide). \"BLS-right: unpaired zeros with Re a > 1/2 pass\" is false for a single real zero. With Theta = (u-a)/(u+a): a = 0.55 gives 335 of ", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Relative to the recalled rank-2 Langlands inner product formula (checked for M = 1 against the direct integral): Gram positivity of truncated minimal-parabolic SL3 Eisenstein series is not closed under Blaschke insertion. A zero of M with 0 < Re a < 1/2 forces a zero at 1 - a (Lemma R, confirmed, valid for a general simple pole p). Measured in addition by this referee: an odd number of real inserted zeros (other than a single zero at 1) fails. Symmetric insertions (zeta times a symmetric polynomial) and non-real conjugate pairs right of 1/2 pass at every tested T >= 0. This is MEASURED twice on different samples (lane: about 4,700 matrices of order up to 5; referee: order-7 matrices plus 3,960 residue-form values per case along the three polar divisors, 0 negative); closure is not proved. DH passes on 400 low-height diagonals and is not shown to fail. At a hypothetical off-line pair, form (*) is confirmed: Q(eta, t_2) is height-independent and positive on a 99 x 34 grid for t_2 >= 0, so it gives no contradiction. Verdict precise-obstruction with a device row stands, with the BLS-right row restricted as above.", "secondReferee": {"by": "c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources", "outcome": "holds with corrections; no PROVED statement broken", "narrowerForm": "see report; nine sentence corrections listed in push/c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources/RESULT.md section 2.3 (not applied in lane files)", "report": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-u6g-scattering-fe-rank2-bridge-stage-a/REFEREE2.md"}}
{"round": 16, "slug": "c16-pos-fe-u2-positivity-rigidity", "kind": "deepen", "verdict": "proved-new-result", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Lemma POS-FE is true, as an identification (score 0). Theorem P: if G = int_[1,inf) x^-s dN with N >= 0, (s-1)G is entire of finite order, and G has zeta's functional equation, then G = r zeta. Proof: the theta relation makes mu = (r/2)delta_0 + even N/2 self-dual; pairing with phi*phi (supp phi in (-1/2,1/2)) gives int |phihat|^2 dN = (r/2)(||phi||^2 - |int phi|^2); phi -> indicator puts N on the integers; periodicity finishes. nu >= 0 enters only via N >= 0. No multiplicativity is used. Each hypothesis is necessary (ZQ: sign; T-NR: mass below 1; G_+: poles), checked numerically. The registered quantitative form implies RH (apply it to zeta). Server screen: with one integer quartet forced, the MILP optimum is ZQ in 40/40 cells (K 25..2000); fractional bound 0.80-0.88 of ZQ. Referee pass is same-lane only; the dense relaxed LP stopped at K=200.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 3, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-pos-fe-u2-positivity-rigidity/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": ["rh-c16zeros-1119211954", "rh-c16checks-1119212035", "rh-c16lpsmall-1119212035", "rh-c16lp2test-1119212237", "rh-c16lp2main-1119213452", "rh-c16lp2wide-1119213452", "rh-c16lpmid2-1119215037", "rh-c16ref-1119214921", "rh-c16reft-1119215148"], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": true, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 1, "newControls": [], "owed": ["independent referee of Theorem P (REFEREE.md is a same-lane pass)", "map: U2-POS closed as identification row in U3 {FE, pole at 1 only, finite order, N >= 0 on [1,inf)}", "STRATEGY 4.0: POS-FE decided; quantitative form recorded as implying RH", "literature check (equality case of the 1-dimensional linear-programming bound)"], "lesson": "With zeta's functional equation, positivity of Lambda acts only through non-negative coefficients of G, and that plus \"no coefficient mass below frequency 1\" is Poisson-summation rigidity (triangle / sinc^2 test function, the 1-dimensional LP-bound equality case). The {FE, POS} class identifies zeta without the Euler product and says nothing about zeros. Fully fractional LP relaxations are uninformative: their minimum falls like 1/K from non-integer multiplicities.", "followUp": "Independent referee of Theorem P (REFEREE.md is a same-lane pass; Steps 4-5 cite classical facts not opened, and no literature search was made). Then enter U2-POS as an identification row in U3 and record in STRATEGY 4.0 that the quantitative form implies RH. lanes_line.json is in the slug directory; campaign/lanes.jsonl was not edited.", "nodes": [], "tags": ["identification", "functional-equation", "positivity", "poisson-summation", "linear-programming-bound", "U2", "U3", "POS-FE", "control-zq", "control-gplus"], "obstructionKind": "identification", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Lemma POS-FE is true. Theorem P (proved): G = int_[1,inf) x^-s dN with N >= 0, (s-1)G entire of finite order, zeta's functional equation => G = r zeta. Proof: theta relation makes mu = (r/2)delta_0 + N/2 (even) self-dual; pairing with phi*phi, supp phi in (-1/2,1/2), gives int |phihat|^2 dN = (r/2)(||phi||^2 - |int phi|^2); phi -> indicator forces N onto the integers; periodicity gives N = r sum delta_n. nu >= 0 enters only through N >= 0 (Bernstein). No multiplicativity used. Each hypothesis necessary: ZQ (sign), T-NR (support below 1), G_+ (poles). Quantitative form QF implies RH (apply to zeta), so it is not a smaller target. Server screen: with one quartet at integer multiplicity the MILP optimum is ZQ in 40 of 40 cells (K 25..2000, eta 0..0.3); fractional lower bound 0.80-0.88 of ZQ.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": true, "allHold": true, "errors": "Theorem P, corollary POS-FE and Proposition T were re-derived step by step (Steps 1-7, scaled form, sharpness example, G_+ positivity) and no error was found in them. Nothing assumes RH or restates verified height. Findings: (E1, error in a side remark labelled PROVED, not used in Theorem P) the Hecke application is inverted: a form on G(lambda) has frequencies sqrt(2n/lambda) in zeta's normalisation, not sqrt(lambda n/2); for lambda > 2 the support starts below 1, so the scaled form does not ap", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Theorem P is proved: if G = int_[1,inf) x^-s dN with N >= 0, (s-1)G entire of finite order, and G has zeta's functional equation, then G = r zeta; POS-FE follows via nu >= 0 => N >= 0 (Bernstein). The proof uses no multiplicativity. Proposition T (balance law int sinc^2 dN+ = int sinc^2 dN-) and the scaled form (support in [a,inf), a > 1 forces G = 0) hold. Each hypothesis is necessary (ZQ: sign; symmetric T-NR: mass below 1, constant 1 sharp; G_+: extra poles). The registered quantitative form implies RH trivially. The server screen (40/40 cells return ZQ; fractional bound 0.80-0.88 of ZQ) stands as a float64 statement on the listed finite column set. Status: identification, score 0, classical in content (one-dimensional LP-bound equality case), new to the campaign record only. Not surviving: the Hecke G(lambda), lambda > 2 corollary (frequency formula inverted) and the word \"new\" beyond the campaign record."}
{"round": 16, "slug": "c16-ctheta-proposition5-power-sum", "kind": "deepen", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Proposition 5 of c15 fails in both directions for arbitrary configurations. PROVED (author only): an infinite lattice row of off-line pairs with spacing d <= 2pi/u adds the constant 2pi/d to the Fejer section for every offset b, so C(theta) cannot see it. PROVED from Turan's second main theorem (recalled, not opened): an isolated cluster of n pairs has b_max <= (c n + O(log log gamma))/(theta log gamma), c between 5.85 and 15.1. MEASURED (ball arithmetic on grids): linear growth in n is attained (rows pass to u b_max = n/2.2, up to e^160); on zeta's ordinates at 1e6-1e9, clusters of 3-40 quadruples pass at 1.6-3.4 times the region for theta=1 and at the strip edge for theta=1/2; theta=1/4 is empty there. PROVED: the region gives C(theta') only with M ~ log^2 t.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 2, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-ctheta-proposition5-power-sum/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": ["rh-c16ct-zeros-1119212702", "rh-c16ct-self-1119212702", "rh-c16ct-univ-1119213051", "rh-c16ct-sign-1119212828", "rh-c16ct-onepair-1119213051", "rh-c16ct-nat-1119213051", "rh-c16ct-real-1119215644", "rh-c16ct-real40-1119222604", "rh-c16ct-floor-1119221320", "rh-c16ct-light-1119221256", "rh-c16ct-ref-1119215624", "rh-c16ct-ball-1119222408", "rh-c16ct-ball2-1119222724", "rh-c16ct-ball3-1119223632", "rh-c16ct-fam-1119222655", "rh-c16ct-ballfam-1119224201", "rh-c16ct-perturb-1119225040"], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": true, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 4, "nodes": ["ctheta-zero-side-correspondence", "lattice-row-invisibility", "turan-isolated-cluster-bound", "fejer-section-band-limit"], "tags": ["deepen", "u7", "ctheta", "proposition-5", "turan", "poisson", "control-zq", "control-tnr", "r4"], "obstructionKind": "statement-too-weak: C(theta) reads off-line zeros only through their local Fourier transform at frequencies <= theta log t; rows of spacing below 2 pi/(theta log t) are invisible, isolated clusters are bounded only by c n/(theta log gamma)", "owed": "independent referee (REFEREE.md is a same-session second pass); map rows Q25/P45 addendum (text in RESULT section 0 item 8); proof or refutation of the finite tapered-row statement; opening the source of Turan's second main theorem", "lesson": "A positivity statement at P = t^theta reads only the band-limited part (frequencies <= theta log t) of the zero measure. Its zero-side reach grows linearly with the local number of off-line pairs and is not a zero-free region; one-pair heuristics overstate what such devices exclude. Passing rows are fine-tuned to about 100 P^(-b) in the ordinates. No step uses multiplicativity; ZQ passes in the window with 3 or more quadruples.", "followUp": "Not a lead for R4. Owed: an independent referee (REFEREE.md is a same-session second pass, no agent tool here); open the source for Turan's theorem; add the Q25/P45 addendum (RESULT section 0 item 8). Unfinished cells: n=16, most n=40, count-preserving rows at 1e9 for theta >= 1/2. Open: proof of the finite tapered-row statement; whether C(theta), theta >= 1/2, confines sets with the exact Riemann-von Mangoldt count (only rows decided). Cores were at 9-10 for about 12 minutes; all units stopped.", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Proposition 5 of c15 is decided for arbitrary configurations: false in both directions as stated. (PROVED) An infinite row of off-line pairs on a lattice of spacing d <= 2 pi/u contributes the constant 2 pi/d to the Fejer section for every offset b (Poisson; T-NR at variable q), so C(theta) carries no information on b for such rows. (PROVED from Turan's second main theorem, recalled) For an isolated cluster of n pairs C(theta) forces b_max <= (c1 n + O(log log gamma))/(theta log gamma), c1 between 5.85 and 15.1. (MEASURED, ball on grids) Linear growth in n is attained: tapered rows pass up to u b_max = n/2.2 (to e^160 in ball arithmetic); added to zeta's on-line ordinates at 1e6-1e9, clusters of 3-40 quadruples pass at 1.6-3.4 times the region for theta=1 and at the strip edge for theta=1/2; theta=1/4 is empty at these heights. (PROVED) The region implies C(theta') only with M ~ log^2 t. Passing rows need ordinates accurate to about 100 P^(-b).", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "Verdict \"precise-obstruction\" stands with scope corrections; no PROVED step failed. Referee file: tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-ctheta-proposition5-power-sum/REFEREE.md (independent pass first, author's self-pass kept below it).\n\nE1 (main): Theorem B is exact only at a fixed u. A row with fixed spacing d and fixed b>0 does not satisfy C(theta) at all heights (the k=1 harmonic appears once theta log t > 2pi/d). What is proved is the window form: ", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Lemma A, Theorem B, Lemma T (given Turan's second main theorem as recalled, for a point set whose entire off-line part is one cluster) and Lemma R are correct. Proposition 5 of c15 is not a two-sided correspondence for arbitrary point sets: (i) PROVED in window form: for each T a lattice row of spacing 2pi/(theta log 2T) contributes the constant 2pi/d for every u <= theta log 2T and every offset, so C(theta) on that window cannot see it (within the Riemann-von Mangoldt density only for theta < 1/2); (ii) PROVED given Turan: an isolated cluster of n pairs has b_max <= (c n + O(log log gamma) + logs of M and r)/(theta log gamma), c between 5.85/(1-kappa) and 15.1; (iii) MEASURED on grids in ball arithmetic: linear growth in n is attained for cos^2 rows of spacing pi/u with n >= about 2.2 u b_max (author to e^160; referee at A=12 and 30 including far field and small u), and clusters of 3 to 40 quadruples added to zeta's ordinates at 1e6-1e9 pass outside the region for theta=1 and at the strip edge for theta=1/2; (iv) PROVED: the region gives C(theta') with M of order log^2 t, and that order is attained in the synthetic class. The all-heights form of the first failure is measured, not proved.", "secondReferee": {"by": "c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources", "outcome": "holds with corrections; no PROVED statement broken", "narrowerForm": "see report; nine sentence corrections listed in push/c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources/RESULT.md section 2.3 (not applied in lane files)", "report": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-ctheta-proposition5-power-sum/REFEREE2.md"}}
{"round": 16, "slug": "c16-qa-filter-silent-cells-geometric-nodes", "kind": "combine", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. The filter is one proposition (Q-P, Q-B, Q-S, Q-A, plus the HEAT question of the lift ruling). Lemma QA (proved): a step reading only the functional equation, poles, order, zero count up to 1 and prime-power atoms is passed by ZQ; twist families by NR-q at every lift value. Also proved: ZQ passes strict compact certificates and heat-box certificates (t >= 0) once the removed pair is high; on the scattering carrier ZQ is Schur with f(u)=f(1-u), given a statement on file. Table: 16 cell rows (3 passed, 4 passed in part, 4 identification classes, 3 with no control on file, 2 with no device); 71 nodes (31 target-level, 25 passed by ZQ, 3 of them only under an unestablished margin, 12 by a recorded control, 3 other). No node is an explore candidate. Twice-read nodes: same class 15 of 15, not blind. REFEREE.md is a same-lane pass; an independent referee is owed.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 2, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-qa-filter-silent-cells-geometric-nodes/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": [], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 4, "newControls": [], "exploreCandidates": ["U3 as an inequality (quantitative POS-FE; step must fail for every density of sup size eps)", "U4 residual (group-law inequality at several points left of Re s = 1, unbounded parameter set)", "U6 (c) Whittaker constants on the double cover of GL(3)", "U6 (e) Bost-Connes states that are not sigma-invariant and not D-invariant", "U6 (f) non-linear functionals of unsummed complex isogenous points"], "owed": ["independent referee (REFEREE.md is a same-lane pass)", "map: Lemma QA data list, Lemma C, BLS note (ZQ has f(z) = f(1-z)), NR-q lift family, scope line of Corollary K for U8 and DN", "second referee on ZQ (STRATEGY item 37) still owed", "Maass-Selberg positivity for ZQ not proved"], "lesson": "Every silent geometric-program node is target-level or passed by a control; ZQ passes finite certificates and atom-only steps inside zeta's own functional-equation class. The five cell rows with no passing control (U3 as an inequality, U4 residual, U6 c, e, f) all read the integers as an additive set (a reading, one reader). A critical-line step must be discontinuous in the coefficient measure at zeta: the margin is zero, f(eps) >= 0.48 sqrt(eps). Sign searches on compact parameter sets (U8, DN canonical tier) sit inside the flow-blindness wall: a survivor there is not a device with R3.", "followUp": "Round-17 explore: take one of the five no-control rows with the entry condition \"name the step that fails for ZQ as its defect tends to 0 and for NR-q at every lift value\". Before any search reports a survivor, add HEAT members at abs(tau) <= 0.005 to its battery. Owed: an independent referee for this lane, a re-read of the five atom-only node rows against their sources, and a proof or refutation of Maass-Selberg positivity for ZQ.", "nodes": [], "tags": ["prefilter", "control-zq", "control-nrq", "Q-A", "U3", "U4", "U6", "U8", "geometric-program", "finite-certificate", "flow-blindness"], "obstructionKind": "control-passes", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Filter F4 (Q-P, Q-B, Q-S, Q-A, Q-H) stated as one proposition. Lemma QA: a step reading only functional equation, poles, order, zero count up to 1 and prime-power atoms is passed by ZQ; for twist families by NR-q at every lift value z. Lemma C: strict conditions on compact sets and heat-flow box certificates (t >= 0) pass to ZQ with the pair high. Lemma R: residue matched by a compound multiplier. On the scattering carrier ZQ is Schur with f(u) = f(1-u) and zeta's archimedean factor (items BLS lacks). Proposition M: zero margin in the coefficient measure, f(eps) >= 0.48 sqrt(eps). Table: 16 cell rows (3 passed, 4 passed in part, 4 identification, 3 no control on file, 2 no device); 71 nodes (31 target-level, 25 passed by ZQ incl. 3 under a margin, 12 by a recorded control, 3 other); none is an explore candidate. 15 twice-read nodes: same class 15 of 15.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "No PROVED step failed; all were re-derived and a fresh numeric run (pairs 10/11, 34/35, 50/51; NR-q at c=2.19; Lemma R on 50/51 with 60/61; new Pick seed) agrees. Corrections, appended as an independent section to tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-qa-filter-silent-cells-geometric-nodes/REFEREE.md (the same-lane pass is kept above it):\nE1: outcome item 2 gives the reach eta(eps) = 0.48 sqrt(eps) \"in the density norm\", but that is the sup term alone. ", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Lemma QA (a), (b), (c) holds: ZQ has data (d1) to (d5) of zeta, and NR-q keeps the functional equation at every lift value z with zeros on Re s = 1/2 +- arccosh(c/2)/log q. Lemma C (i) and (ii) for t >= 0, Lemma R (with the disjointness side condition), Proposition M in its sup-norm form (reach 0.48 sqrt(eps)), and J2, J3, K hold. M_ZQ is Schur unconditionally, a standard fact for any such f. The 16-row cell table and 71-row node table are internally consistent readings by one reader (31 target-level, 25 passed by ZQ including 3 under an unestablished margin, 12 by a recorded control, 3 other; no node is an explore candidate). Not surviving as written: the reach eta(eps) in the norm p, and the additive-carrier pattern for all five explore candidates (it covers U3-1 to U3-3 and U6 (c), (e), (f), not the U4 residual). Verdict precise-obstruction stands as a filter and a table.", "secondReferee": {"by": "c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources", "outcome": "holds with corrections; no PROVED statement broken", "narrowerForm": "see report; nine sentence corrections listed in push/c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources/RESULT.md section 2.3 (not applied in lane files)", "report": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-qa-filter-silent-cells-geometric-nodes/REFEREE2.md"}}
{"round": 16, "slug": "c16-dn-canonical-tier-ball-conversion", "kind": "compute", "verdict": "dead", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Registered outcome \"none\" holds. All 67,138 float64-undecided nodes of the canonical tier {T-NR, E_a, HEAT} of dictionary DN are decided in balls (128 to 1024 bits): 360 reflection-identity, 37,634 excluded (HEAT never rejectable), 29,144 at T-train, 0 undecided; 0 hold out under the c15 rule or a threshold-optimised read (held-out T-NR at most 1 of 24 opposite). Extension: the 22,508 float64 T-train nodes confirmed; 86 one-kernel nodes pass the threshold-optimised hold-out and are refuted: 75 to 93 of 350 characters of conductor up to 60 lie on the controls' side. c14 DJ recount, canonical lifts: 59 T-train, 0 full; 15,351 open rows excluded in balls. First check 200 of 200; J1 ties and nonzero kernels pass. c15's \"undecided at 1024 bits\" was an acceptance-floor artefact. MEASURED; server was overloaded, 68% of nodes ran in local helper runs (stated). Referee is the author's second pass.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 2, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-dn-canonical-tier-ball-conversion/RESULT.md", "heavy": true, "serverUnits": ["rh-c16dn-repro-1119212327", "rh-c16dn-repro-1119212349", "rh-c16dn-c14count-1119212349", "rh-c16dn-c14ball-1119213706", "rh-c16dn-main-1119213705", "rh-c16dn-main2-1119215038", "rh-c16dn-feas-1120000344"], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": true, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 0, "nodes": ["noncone-kernel-separator", "joint-zeta-twist-pair"], "tags": ["compute", "prereg", "certified-conversion", "ball-arithmetic", "kernel-sign-functional", "log-difference", "canonical-tier", "control-heat", "control-tnr", "control-ea", "dictionary-DN", "dictionary-DJ", "family-34"], "obstructionKind": "finite-search-none, ball-certified at the formerly undecided nodes; far-tail log differences of zeta and of backward heat with polar terms are doubly exponentially small and ordered so that HEAT is never rejectable in second differences; where the three training classes are rejected (third differences) held-out T-NR members at larger split primes stay on the positives' side; threshold-optimised survivors of a one-kernel family fail on characters of conductor 31 to 60", "owed": "independent referee (REFEREE.md is the author's second pass with separate mpmath code); map row G41 wording as proposed in RESULT section 11; correction of the c15 line '85 of 600 not decided at 1024 bits'; strict tail term in ballk.BHeat._integrand; FE tier of DN not re-read; quotient minors and product families have no ball stage", "lesson": "Use a relative acceptance test for balls: an absolute floor made 256-bit balls containing 0 count as decided. A hold-out read at one fixed threshold hides nodes that pass at another, and held-out positives repeating the zeta kernel do not test one-signedness; A-only families need a full character set.", "followUp": "None as a lead. Record map row G41 (DN final, canonical tier closed as MEASURED) and the c15 correction; an independent referee is owed; FE tier of DN, quotient minors and product families were not re-read in balls.", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Registered outcome 'none' (prediction holds). Certified conversion of the canonical tier {T-NR, E_a, HEAT} of dictionary DN (c15): the 67,138 float64-undecided nodes are all decided in python-flint balls (ladder 128/256/512, extended 1024): 360 reflection-identity, 37,634 excluded (HEAT never rejectable), 29,144 at T-train, 0 undecided; 0 hold out under the c15 rule and 0 under a threshold-optimised read (held-out T-NR at most 1 of 24 opposite). Extension: the 22,508 float64 T-train nodes confirmed in balls, 0 hold out under the c15 rule; 86 one-kernel nodes (third log difference of the kernel with polar terms) pass the threshold-optimised hold-out and are refuted on the positive side: 75 to 93 of 350 primitive characters of conductor <= 60 lie on the controls' side. c14 dictionary DJ recount for the canonical lifts: 59 T-train (the FE-tier rows), 0 full; 15,351 float64-open rows all excluded in balls. The c15 report 'not decided at 1024 bits' was an artefact of an absolute acceptance floor (256-bit balls containing 0 accepted).", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "Outcome \"none\" confirmed; no count in the RESULT table changes. Errors and overstatements found: (1) A1 \"status in balls: 22,508 of 22,508\" is not what the code does: cball.resolve exits at round 0 when the float64 status is already T-train, before any ball entry; all 6,724 b5l-with rows of feas.json have nb=0/maxprec=0, and the 192,610 b2-with ball entries come from hold-out reads only. The 22,508 nodes keep their c15 float64 status; ball confirmation of a float64 T-train status exists only for", "surviving": "MEASURED, no statement about zeros of zeta. On the registered c15 node set of dictionary DN, canonical tier {T-NR, E_a, HEAT}, the 67,138 float64-undecided family-nodes are decided with ball arithmetic at the entries that matter (360 reflection-identity; 37,634 excluded with HEAT not rejectable; 29,144 T-train; 0 undecided) and none holds out under the c15 rule or the threshold-scanned read. The 22,508 float64 T-train nodes keep their float64 status (not ball-confirmed), 0 hold out under the c15 rule; 86 b2-with nodes pass the threshold-scanned hold-out and are refuted on the positive side (75 to 93 of 350 primitive characters of conductor up to 60 on the controls' side; reproduced independently for Legendre characters mod 43, 47, 59). DJ canonical lifts: 59 T-train, 0 full, 15,351 open rows excluded in balls (stored outputs consistent, not re-run). The c15 \"not decided at 1024 bits\" was an acceptance-floor artefact (confirmed in code). Verdict dead; outcome \"none\".", "secondReferee": {"by": "c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources", "outcome": "holds with corrections; no PROVED statement broken", "narrowerForm": "see report; nine sentence corrections listed in push/c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources/RESULT.md section 2.3 (not applied in lane files)", "report": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-dn-canonical-tier-ball-conversion/REFEREE2.md"}}
{"round": 16, "slug": "c16-amplifier-below-truncation-eisw-compute", "kind": "compute", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Family 31 item \"amplifier with T < N\" closes. PROVED: T_m on the truncated Eisenstein series is lambda(m) f minus pseudo-Eisenstein series cut at heights Td/a; coset c enters the pairing of cuts h_i, h_j iff c^2 h_i h_j < 1; closed Gram formula for all T, N (matches quadrature to 1e-14). MEASURED (arb balls): optimal gain below N^delta in all 132 registered zero cells (max 0.9919), 844 rows at zeros 1-300, 463 formal rows; crossing terms change it by a factor in [0.987, 1.0094]. Not proved for all N. EIS-w exceeds N^delta in 394 of 528 rows and obeys the same general comparator. Registered prediction R2 <= 1 FAILED for T < N (sup up to 1.46, float64); PROVED cap R2 <= M/L; EIS-w shows the same excess. The registered stage-A clause fired literally; set aside with reasons. No independent referee; (1,512) probe unfinished.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 2, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-amplifier-below-truncation-eisw-compute/RESULT.md", "resultFile": true, "heavy": false, "serverUnits": ["rh-c16amp-grid-1119212532", "rh-c16amp-s2-1119212827", "rh-c16amp-extz-1119214756", "rh-c16amp-extn-1119214756", "rh-c16amp-n512-1119220012", "rh-c16amp-formal-1119220025"], "restatement": false, "prereg": "PREREG.md; P-A at zeros held; P-A at EIS-w points failed as the author's registered expectation said; S2 prediction R2 <= 1 failed; the registered clause 'R2 > 1 names a stage-A candidate' fired and is set aside in RESULT.md with reasons (proved cap, control shares the effect)", "controls": "EIS-w run (528 + 841 + 69 rows): passes every step, exceeds N^delta, shares the lower-side excess under the same cap; BLS, T-NR, E_a not run; DH, sign twists, U, THIN, heat, theta^w, transfer operator, Beurling not formulable", "proposedRow": "G42 (RESULT.md section 9), extends the c15 row of family 31", "notCovered": "a proof of G_opt <= N^delta for T < N; N above 128 at T = 1; uniformity of M/L in the height and at hypothetical zeros with small delta; BLS on the crossing terms", "laneRefereeNote": "same-agent second pass only (REFEREE.md, separate code paths: quadrature Gram against arb rows 3.7e-11, crossing formula against mpmath 3.9e-17); independent referee owed before any row is entered in the map", "owed": "independent referee; decision on the registered S2 clause", "lesson": "Below the truncation height Hecke operators stop acting by dilation and coset terms cross the truncation line, but the effect is a bounded constant: under 1 per cent on the gain, and on the lower side at most the mass fraction the unamplified inequality drops below y = 1. EIS-w shares both. A pre-registered decision clause needs the control comparison written into it.", "followUp": "Independent referee for Lemma U, Proposition CAP and the decision to set aside the registered S2 clause (REFEREE.md is a same-agent second pass); lane line is in lane_line.json in the slug directory, not appended to campaign/lanes.jsonl. Optional: prove or refute G_opt <= N^delta for T < N (margin at zero 1 shrinks with N).", "nodes": [], "tags": ["compute", "family-31", "eisenstein-edge", "hecke-amplifier", "maass-selberg", "eis-w", "prereg"], "obstructionKind": "identity up to a bounded constant: amplified norm exact; gain bounded by N^delta at zeros; lower-side improvement capped by M/L", "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 3, "brokenProved": 0, "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Hecke amplifier of length N above the truncation height T on the truncated Eisenstein series E*(z, rho/2). PROVED: T_m on the truncated series is lambda(m) f minus pseudo-Eisenstein series cut at heights Td/a; the coset c enters the pairing of cuts h_i, h_j iff c^2 h_i h_j < 1; closed Gram formula for all T, N (checked against quadrature to 1e-14). MEASURED (arb balls): optimal gain below N^delta in all 132 registered zero cells (T in {1,2,4}, N up to 32T; max 0.9919), in 844 rows at zeros 1-300 and 463 formal rows with delta down to 0.01; crossing terms change the gain by a factor in [0.987, 1.0094]. EIS-w exceeds N^delta in 394 of 528 rows and obeys the same general comparator MS(T)/MS(T/N). Lower side: registered prediction R2 <= 1 FAILED for T < N (sup R2 up to 1.46 at N <= 8); PROVED cap R2 <= M/L = 1/(1 - S/M); EIS-w shows the same excess. Constants only; no stage-A candidate recommended.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "No PROVED step fails. Lemma U (a)-(d), formula (U2)/(G), Proposition T, Proposition CAP and the T >= N comparator were re-derived by hand and confirmed. Referee numerics (local, memcap 8 GB): (i) new test: formula (G) satisfies the Hecke relations P[m,n] = sum_{d|(m,n)} P[mn/d^2,1] to 1.5e-82 at 4 points x T in {1, 3/2, 2, 7/3}, N = 24; (ii) (U2) against the defining (x,y) double integral in 32 new cases, 2.1e-14; (iii) new cells (3,12), (3/2,9), (1,16), (1,64): G_opt/N^delta between 0.923 and 0", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta. PROVED: on the truncated Eisenstein series, T_m Lambda^T f = lambda(m) f minus pseudo-Eisenstein series cut at heights Td/a; coset c enters the pairing of cuts h_i, h_j iff c^2 h_i h_j < 1; closed Gram formula (G) for all T >= 1, N, sigma != 1 (agrees with quadrature to 7e-14 and satisfies the Hecke relations to 1e-82); R2 = 1 for T >= N; R2 <= M/L (a validity statement, not a structural limit). MEASURED (arb balls): G_opt < N^delta at on-line zeros in every computed row with T <= 4, N <= 128, gamma <= 541, and in 463 formal rows with delta >= 0.01 at t <= 56.5; crossing factor within [0.987, 1.0094]. MEASURED (float64): sup R2 between 1.04 and 1.46 for T < N, N <= 8, also at EIS-w points. OPEN: G_opt <= N^delta for all N with T < N; the large-height small-delta regime; boundedness of M/L. Family 31 item \"T < N\": no gain beyond N^delta found in the stated range; a measured obstruction on that range, not a proved closure. The registered stage-A clause fired and its disposition needs a decision outside the lane.", "secondReferee": {"by": "c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources", "outcome": "holds with corrections; no PROVED statement broken", "narrowerForm": "see report; nine sentence corrections listed in push/c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources/RESULT.md section 2.3 (not applied in lane files)", "report": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-amplifier-below-truncation-eisw-compute/REFEREE2.md"}}
{"round": 16, "slug": "c16-referee-r15-j1prime-u8-screening", "kind": "repair", "verdict": "partial-result", "claim": "Referee lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta. Round-15 lanes 1 to 6: every PROVED statement re-derived, none broken, each holds with corrections (K1 of the Klein lane and the measured kernel-search outcome not redone). Control ZQ: functional equation, atoms, defect bound and Lemma L with the pole clause hold on two new zero pairs. Lemma J1' holds as stated. The U8 heat-inheritance exclusion holds and is one case of Lemma H (new, one referee): a monomial bound M<=lam is inherited by every tau<0 iff lam*S>=0 or M*lam<=0, otherwise exactly for |tau|<=4|log(lam/M)|/|S|. A U8 search may run in round 17 only restricted (three or more terms, tau* column). Screening sample: recomputed numbers agree except one sampled Haar-variance column (1.63 against exact 1.5905); the T-NR claim holds for functionals of the on-line list alone; \"four kinds of separation\" is false as worded (a fifth kind occurs). Eleven false sentences listed. Davenport-Heilbronn recomputed to T=1e4 only (server overloaded).", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c16-referee-r15-j1prime-u8-screening/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": ["rh-c16ref-1119212121", "rh-c16ref2-1119214854"], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 2, "refereedItems": {"c15-edge-argument-strip-width-hecke-amplified": {"ruling": "holds with corrections", "referees": 2}, "c15-control-with-zeta-fe-classes-u1-u2": {"ruling": "holds with corrections", "referees": 2}, "c15-u5-window-count-threshold-translate-control": {"ruling": "holds with corrections", "referees": 2}, "c15-u7-growing-section-twin-ladder-bridge": {"ruling": "holds with corrections", "referees": 2}, "c15-nonhomogeneous-pair-triple-kernel-search": {"ruling": "PROVED lemmas hold; counts corrected; measured outcome not rerun", "referees": 2}, "c15-klein-transport-lemma-w-stage-a-and-e1": {"ruling": "holds with corrections (W1-W3, E1'); K1 not re-derived", "referees": 2}, "control ZQ (FE, atoms, defect bound, Lemma L with pole clause)": {"ruling": "holds with corrections", "referees": 2}, "Lemma J1' (LIFT_RULING section 5)": {"ruling": "holds", "referees": 2}, "U8 heat-inheritance exclusion": {"ruling": "holds; extended to Lemma H (one referee)", "referees": 2}, "s1-zero-statistics-gram": {"ruling": "holds with corrections", "referees": 1}, "s1-scattering-one-line": {"ruling": "holds with corrections", "referees": 1}, "s1-prime-torus-orbit": {"ruling": "holds with corrections; one numeric column not reproduced", "referees": 1}}, "falseSentences": 11, "u8SearchRound17": "may run, restricted: monomial, two-term and equal-S functionals removed (Lemma H); HEAT column from zeta values with tau* recorded; tau ladder below 0.02; ball arithmetic for margins; polar-term readings registered separately", "tags": ["referee", "repair", "control-ZQ", "lemma-L", "lemma-J1prime", "U8", "backward-heat", "monomial-inequality", "screening-arm", "T-NR", "davenport-heilbronn"], "obstructionKind": "none (referee lane)", "lesson": "For kernels without polar terms the backward-heat member is a pointwise Gaussian multiple, so the HEAT column of any polynomial functional is fixed by zeta's own values: F_tau = sum a_j exp(tau S_j/4) M_j. A finite-node inequality with positive margin passes all small |tau|; only a threshold tuned inside zeta's margin rejects a registered HEAT class. Screening summaries must list \"coefficients alone\" as a kind of separation. All six round-15 lanes already had one independent referee; for lanes 2, 4, 5 my pass was not blind to it.", "followUp": "Get a second referee for Lemma H, then register the restricted U8 compute item (monomial, two-term and equal-S functionals removed; tau* column; tau ladder below 0.02; ball margins) before any run; apply the eleven corrected sentences, two of them in STRATEGY section 0b.", "laneClaim": "Independent referee lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta; R4 not addressed. Round-15 lanes 1 to 6: every statement labelled PROVED re-derived, none broken, each holds with corrections (second independent referee; K1 of the Klein lane and the measured kernel-search outcome not redone). Control ZQ: functional equation, atoms, bound 8e^-2(eta^2+d^2)/(1/2-eta)^2 and Lemma L with the pole clause hold on two new zero pairs. Lemma J1' holds as stated. The U8 heat-inheritance exclusion holds and is one case of Lemma H (new, one referee): a monomial bound M<=lam on a kernel without polar terms is inherited by every tau<0 iff lam*S>=0 or M*lam<=0, otherwise exactly for |tau|<=4|log(lam/M)|/|S|; a U8 search may run in round 17 restricted to functionals of three or more terms, HEAT column computed from zeta's values alone. Screening sample (3 lanes): recomputed numbers agree except one sampled Haar-variance column (1.63 against exact 1.5905); 'same value on zeta and T-NR' holds for functionals of the on-line list alone; 'four kinds of separation' is false as worded: a fifth kind (coefficients alone) occurs. Eleven sentences false as written are listed.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "No PROVED statement broken. Re-derived by hand: Lemma J1', J1'', Lemma H (H1-H4) with (C1)-(C5), ZQ functional equation, density D, defect bound, Lemma L with the pole clause, the Klein row 1.6 inequality and W1 numbers, edge row 1.1, u7 closed form / Lemma 2 / Lemma 3, u5 Lemma 4, the counts, T-NR closed forms, Haar variance formula. Own numerics on new cases all agree: Lemma H at kernel level on 1,500 random monomials (0 mismatches), ZQ on zeros 150/151 with eta=0.2, DH off-line zero and 302 o", "surviving": "Referee lane, no attack, nothing about zeros of zeta, score 0. Lemma J1' holds as stated. The U8 heat-inheritance exclusion holds and is one case of Lemma H, which now has two derivations: for a real kernel without polar terms a monomial bound M<=lam is inherited by every tau<0 iff lam*S>=0 or M*lam<=0, otherwise exactly for |tau|<=4|log(lam/M)|/|S|; corollaries (C1)-(C4) hold. A restricted U8 search (three or more terms with distinct S_j, tau* column recorded) is a recommendation, not a theorem. Control ZQ: functional equation, atoms plus absolutely continuous density D, bound 8e^-2(eta^2+d^2)/(1/2-eta)^2 (and 8), and Lemma L with the pole clause hold, confirmed on a third new zero pair. The round-15 rulings I re-derived stand, except that the corrected sentence for the translate lane must read: the reflected translate has defect (L+2|delta|)^2/(8T), |delta|<=pi/(2 log(T/2 pi)) depending on T, with L^2/(8T) a lower bound and the crossover at 8 pi/log(T/2 pi) only an upper limit. Screening: the exact Haar variance is 1.5905 (not 1.63); the T-NR claim holds for functionals of the on-line list alone; the DH numbers to T=1e4 reproduce.", "nodes": []}
{"round": 17, "slug": "c17-u6e-bost-connes-non-invariant-state-twin-ladder", "kind": "explore", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Cell U6 (e) closes at the first lemma; no independent referee yet. Lemma G: omega -> omega(b* . b)/omega(b* b), b invertible, maps states to states; T-NR (b = D^(1/2)), finite DEL and gauge twins have this form, so positivity of no state separates them from zeta. Lemma E: mu*-eigenstates omega(x mu_m*) = m^-s omega(x) exist for all Re s > 0 and read only n^-s plus local factors, or L(beta, chi)/zeta(beta) at real beta > 1. Lemma K: kernels <xi_w, X xi_s> read arguments with real part > 1. Lemma T: two eigenstates on Re s = beta/2 are at norm distance 2 sqrt(1 - |zeta(beta + i tau)|^2/zeta(beta)^2) for beta > 1 and exactly 2 for beta <= 1. DEL and E_a pass every step. Checks at 30 digits (mpmath, local); server not used.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 2, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-u6e-bost-connes-non-invariant-state-twin-ladder/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": [], "nodes": ["connes-twin-ladder-crosswalk", "mem-semilocal-fourier-fs"], "tags": ["bost-connes", "non-invariant-state", "eigenstate", "kakutani", "T-NR", "DEL", "U6e", "D8"], "obstructionKind": "read set right of 1; state positivity invariant under conjugation by invertible elements; product-state overlap is 0 for beta <= 1", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 5, "lesson": "State positivity is invariant under conjugation by any invertible element, so twins of the form b xi (T-NR, finite DEL) can be rejected only by an exact relation, never by positivity. The overlap of two product-vector states is either the convergent Euler product or 0: for beta <= 1 the states are orthogonal, so no function of tau remains that could read a zero.", "followUp": "Independent referee for Lemmas G, E, T (Lemma T uses irreducibility of the Toeplitz tensor product, stated not opened); then enter sub-row D8 (vi) and mark cell U6 (e) closed for positivity reads, residual = Weil-form weights (rows P1, G21).", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Cell U6 (e) closes at the first lemma. Lemma G: omega -> omega(b* . b)/omega(b* b), b invertible, maps states to states with equivalent GNS representation; T-NR (b = D^(1/2)), finite DEL and gauge twins are of this form, so positivity of no state separates them from zeta. Lemma E: mu*-eigenstates omega(x mu_m*) = m^-s omega(x) exist for all Re s > 0, are classified by a KMS_{2 Re s} measure and read only n^-s plus local factors or L(beta, chi)/zeta(beta) at real beta > 1. Lemma K: kernels <xi_w, X xi_s> read arguments with real part > 1 and are positive iff X >= 0. Lemma T: two eigenstates on Re s = beta/2 are at norm distance 2 sqrt(1 - |zeta(beta + i tau)|^2/zeta(beta)^2) for beta > 1 and exactly 2 for beta <= 1 (Kakutani dichotomy). DEL and E_a pass every step.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "Verdict (precise obstruction, no statement about zeros) holds. All PROVED steps (Lemmas G, E, K, T, S(a,c,d), N4) re-derived and confirmed; no RH assumption, no restated verified height. Corrections, none changing a conclusion: E1 (display error, sec 3.3(b)): the adjoint is V_n* g(x) = n^-s g(nx), not n^-conj(s) g(nx), so V_m* 1 = m^-s 1; the final formula Omega_s(mu_n x mu_m*) = n^-conj(s) m^-s nu(x) is correct only with the corrected adjoint (numerically: n^-s form agrees to 3e-32, the printed", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Cell U6 (e) closes at the first lemma as a precise obstruction: (1) for every state omega on the Bost-Connes algebra A and invertible b, omega(b* . b)/omega(b* b) is a state in the same GNS representation (classical); T-NR in the conjugation form b = D^(1/2), finite DEL and the gauge twins have this form, so positivity of a state does not separate them from zeta. (2) mu*-eigenstates omega(x mu_m*) = m^-s omega(x) exist for every Re s > 0 (on L^2(Z^, nu_beta), with adjoint V_n* g = n^-s g(n.)); on the algebraic Hecke algebra they read n^-conj(s), m^-s and finitely many local factors, or L(beta, chi)/zeta(beta) at real beta > 1; on absolutely summable elements every zeta-argument has real part > 1. (3) Kernels <xi_w, X xi_s> read zeta(conj(w)+s; r) with real part > 1 and are positive semidefinite iff X >= 0. (4) Two eigenstates on Re s = beta/2 are at norm distance 2 sqrt(1 - |zeta(beta+i tau)|^2/zeta(beta)^2) (vector states, beta > 1) and exactly 2 for beta <= 1, also for DEL, THIN, U, the T-NR twin and E_a. DEL (finite S) and E_a pass every step. Open: states cut out by other exact relations, normal states of the type III_1 factor beyond the three families, general elements of the norm closure.", "secondReferee": {"by": "c18-referee-r17-independent-sources", "outcome": "holds with corrections; no PROVED statement broken", "narrowerForm": "see report and push/c18-referee-r17-independent-sources/GATE.md (window law: Remark K for the unwindowed device only; E_a row decided on its own configuration; W4 density form, W5 second bullet ARGUED)", "report": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-u6e-bost-connes-non-invariant-state-twin-ladder/REFEREE2.md"}}
{"round": 17, "slug": "c17-repair-owed-record-r16-cell-nodes", "kind": "repair", "verdict": "partial-result", "claim": "Record lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta; headline unchanged at 1 of 4. The eleven silent-* nodes are now node type 'cell' (U2-POS closed, U6 (g) tried-not-closed, nine cells) and generate.py gives them no device weight and no waived penalty: top 60 with an open device 57 -> 0, floored only 3 -> 60, closed 0 -> 0. Map 205 -> 208 rows (D10, P56, G42), with G41, Q30, P45, S12b and the BLS notes edited. STRATEGY 0b, 3.1 (items 42-47) and 4.0 updated. S2 disposition recorded. No round-16 outcome record was missing; merge_outcomes.py not run. Every changed number is attributed in ENGINE_LOG. Not done in place: nine of the eleven corrected sentences sit in lane files outside the edit scope; they are in the map and campaign/CORRECTIONS_R16.md. Literature rescan found no 2611 preprint; four identifiers not on file are listed, none opened. No independent referee has read this lane.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-repair-owed-record-r16-cell-nodes/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": [], "nodes": [], "tags": ["repair", "record", "cell-node-type", "generator", "map-rows"], "obstructionKind": "record", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 0, "lesson": "With the cells out of the device pool the generator has no open device node: all 60 top entries stand on the one floored 7/8 device type, so it cannot name the next explore slot. A record lane limited to engine/, campaign/ and the map cannot correct sentences in lane files. Other lanes wrote lanes.jsonl and outcomes/ during the run, so scoreboard changes needed an attribution run on the pre-lane inputs.", "followUp": "Independent referee for this lane: check rows D10, P56, G42 against their sources (G42's T >= N half was written from the claim line and second-referee table, not a full read of the c15 lane) and the reading of 'scored as a tag' (cell nodes still enter as open-lemma members: 2 of the top 60). Then dated correction notes in the nine lane files, and revise cell U6 (g) / row D10 when c17-rank2-gram-symmetric-blaschke-closure reports.", "owed": "independent referee; correction notes in nine lane files; U6 (g) state after the round-17 closure lane; second referees for round-16 lanes 1, 3, 4, 5, 6", "laneClaim": "Record lane, no attack, nothing about zeros of zeta; the headline does not move. (1) The eleven silent-* nodes are read classes of node type 'cell' (engine/curated/devices.json, key cells; U2-POS closed, U6 (g) tried-not-closed, nine cells); generate.py gives a cell no device weight and no waived penalty. Top 60: with an open device 57 -> 0, floored only 3 -> 60, closed 0 -> 0; 2 entries keep a cell node as a tagged open-lemma member; device types 53 closed / 1 floored / 0 open. (2) Map 205 -> 208 rows (D10 rank-2 Gram positivity for U6 (g), tried not closed; P56 Theorem P identification for U2-POS; G42 Hecke amplification with the family-31 note 'measured obstruction on T <= 4, N <= 128'); G41 canonical tier closed as MEASURED; Q30/P45 addendum; BLS note corrected and BLS in rank 2 with the restricted BLS-right form; seven rows in section 7. STRATEGY: section 4.0 entry for POS-FE, section 3.1 items 42 to 47, two sentences of section 0b corrected. The other nine corrected sentences stand in lane files outside the edit scope; they are in the map and in campaign/CORRECTIONS_R16.md. (3) Fired clause S2 of the amplifier lane: set aside; no control comparison in the clause; EIS-w shares the excess; no follow-up lane. (4) All eight round-16 lanes had outcome records; none written; merge_outcomes.py not run. (5) Engine and scoreboard rerun at baseline, after the cell change and at the end; every changed number attributed in ENGINE_LOG. (6) Literature rescan: no 2611 preprint on zero-free regions or the 7/8 abscissa found; four identifiers not on file listed, none opened.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "Verdict holds; the lane has no PROVED step of its own. Engine counts were reproduced by rerunning build_graph.py, generate.py and scoreboard.py on a scratch copy (graph byte-identical; CANDIDATES identical except the dump path; scoreboard identical except the timestamp). Seven corrections, none changing a count, state or verdict. E1 (literature line misleading): \"no 2611 preprint found\" describes one unlogged search; the campaign files already hold at least 14 identifiers 2611.*, three of them o", "surviving": "Record lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta; headline unchanged at 1 of 4. The eleven silent-* nodes are cells in engine/curated/devices.json (U2-POS closed, U6 (g) tried-not-closed, nine cells) with field and role 'cell' in the graph (graph node type unchanged: open-direction); generate.py gives them no device weight and no waived penalty. Top 60 with an open device 57 -> 0, floored only 3 -> 60, closed 0 -> 0 (reproduced; forced by five floored nodes times the per-device cap of 12, a statement about the generator, not about leads). Map 205 -> 208 rows (D10, P56, G42) with G41, Q30, P45, S12b and the BLS notes edited; rows agree with their referee files except that G42 carries \"394 of 528\" without its referee's restriction. STRATEGY 0b, 3.1 (items 42 to 47, of which 45 and 47 are not closures) and 4.0 updated. S2 disposition recorded. No round-16 outcome record was missing; merge_outcomes.py not run. Changed numbers are attributed in ENGINE_LOG; in RESULT section 5 the increase 861 -> 988 is 117 from s2-* files and 10 from the c17-u6e line. Nine of the eleven corrected sentences remain uncorrected in lane files and are in the map and campaign/CORRECTIONS_R16.md. Literature: one search returned no 2611 identifier and missed three already on file; it is not evidence about new preprints; four identifiers not on file are listed, none opened. One independent referee (this pass)."}
{"round": 17, "slug": "c17-u6f-isogenous-points-norm-jensen-gap", "kind": "deepen", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "Cell U6 (f) is closed for the three non-linear reads of the p^2+p-2 complex isogenous points of theta; nothing about zeros of zeta. (N) Proved: norm = theta(x)^(p^2+p)/(theta(x/p^2) theta(p^2 x)), an identity in the dilation module of log theta with Mellin multiplier p^2+p-p^(2u)-p^(-2u) on zeta(u)zeta(u+1) (checked to 1e-300 at 200 points, p = 3..13). (J) Proved: the Jensen gap is negative on the whole arc, limit log(p/(p+2)); it follows from the sum identity, the norm identity and monotonicity. Epstein theta(x)theta(nx), n = 5, 6, passes at inert primes (proved); the T-NR twins fail the norm identity and J<0 at p = 3, 11 (certified signs). Zeta enters M[J] additively, 1e-10 to 1e-15 of M[J] at |t| = 200 (measured, error not enclosed). (D) Proved: discriminant sign is (-1)^((p+2)(p-1)/2) for every real function. Not refereed; several controls not run or not formulable.", "aboutZeros": false, "refHolds": true, "referees": 2, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "errors": "No PROVED step failed. Minor corrections only (none changes the verdict): (1) Lemma D is the classical discriminant sign rule (-1)^(number of non-real conjugate pairs) and should be labelled CLASSICAL, not presented as proved-new. (2) Section 4 row E_a: real point values make the paired values coincide, so D = 0 identically, not \"D >= 0 differing from the parity value\". (3) Section 4 \"identifies f up to the finite list of such eta quotients\" is asserted without proof or citation (unused; should ", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": ["rh-c17u6f-smoke-1120003847", "rh-c17u6f-grid-1120003902", "rh-c17u6f-gridx-1120004101", "rh-c17u6f-mellin-1120004433"], "obstructionKind": "module identity (N); corollary of two identities and monotonicity, passed by Epstein at inert primes (J); parity count (D)", "lesson": "For a Hecke eigenform with a product formula, both the sum and the product of the values at the isogenous points are dilation-module quantities on the arc, so any read built from the mean and the norm is a pointwise function of dilates. Epstein forms pass such reads prime by prime at inert primes; the discriminant sign is a parity count.", "followUp": "One independent referee of Lemmas N, J, D and the Epstein-at-inert-primes corollary (REFEREE_REQUEST.md in the lane directory), then record the proposed wording in map row G33. No further attack on this cell; the only reads left open are symmetric functions of degree 3 or more of the point values, with no candidate inequality.", "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-u6f-isogenous-points-norm-jensen-gap/RESULT.md", "laneClaim": "Cell U6 (f) closed for three non-linear reads of the p^2+p-2 complex isogenous points of theta under T_{p^2}; nothing about zeros of zeta. (N) norm = theta(x)^(p^2+p)/(theta(x/p^2) theta(p^2 x)) (proved; 1e-300 at 200 points, p = 3..13): identity in the dilation module of log theta, Mellin multiplier p^2+p-p^(2u)-p^(-2u) on zeta(u) zeta(u+1) times a 2-adic factor. (J) Jensen gap < 0 on the whole arc, limit log(p/(p+2)) (proved from sum identity, norm identity, monotonicity); Epstein theta(x)theta(nx), n = 5, 6, passes at inert primes (proved), T-NR twins fail the norm identity and J<0 at p = 3, 11 (certified signs). Zeta enters M[J] additively, 1e-10 to 1e-15 of M[J] at |t| = 200 (measured). (D) sign = (-1)^((p+2)(p-1)/2) for every real function (proved).", "surviving": "For odd p, the three non-linear reads of the p^2+p-2 complex isogenous points of theta under T_{p^2} on the arc reduce as follows: the norm equals theta(x)^(p^2+p)/(theta(x/p^2) theta(p^2 x)), a dilation-module identity with Mellin multiplier p^2+p-p^(2u)-p^(-2u) on M[log theta] = pi^(-u) Gamma(u) zeta(u) zeta(u+1)(2-2^(-u))(1-2^(1-u)); the Jensen gap is negative on the whole arc with limit log(p/(p+2)) at the cusp, as a consequence of the sum identity, the norm identity and monotonicity; the discriminant sign is the parity (-1)^((p+2)(p-1)/2) for every function with real coefficients (classical rule). The Epstein control theta(x)theta(nx), n = 5, 6, passes all three at inert primes (proved; reconfirmed numerically at p = 17), and the T-NR twins fail the norm identity and fail J<0 at p = 3 and 11. Zeta enters M[J_p] only additively, 1e-10.5 to 1e-15 of M[J_p] at t = 200 (measured, reproduced independently, error not enclosed). Cell U6 (f) is closed for these three reads; nothing about zeros of zeta.", "refereeHolds": true, "nodes": [], "tags": [], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0, "secondReferee": {"by": "c18-referee-r17-independent-sources", "outcome": "holds with corrections; no PROVED statement broken", "narrowerForm": "see report and push/c18-referee-r17-independent-sources/GATE.md (window law: Remark K for the unwindowed device only; E_a row decided on its own configuration; W4 density form, W5 second bullet ARGUED)", "report": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-u6f-isogenous-points-norm-jensen-gap/REFEREE2.md"}}
{"round": 17, "slug": "c17-u3-inequality-discontinuity-functional", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "The U3 inequality is target-level in all three relaxation directions, and multiplicativity enters none of them. No statement about zeros of zeta. PROVED (elementary, unrefereed): the defect enters Theorem P at Step 6 as int sinc^2 F = 0, Lipschitz with constant 0.0486; the square root comes from reality on the critical line (double zeros). Frequencies within delta: zeta times symmetric T-NR at q = 1+delta has exact FE, N >= 0, and zeros at 1/2 +- b for any b, first at height pi/delta. NR-q is multiplicative on its semigroup, so it fails only through integrality; a local-root bound gives f(delta) = delta, the factor's own zeros. MEASURED (float64, model-dependent): minimal FE defect for a quartet is delta_0(pair) + kappa eta^2, at least 0.047 below height 125, so reach is 0 at delta <= 1e-2 in both classes; multiplicative/unconstrained ratio 1.003 to 1.40. The unconstrained LP at X = 4000 did not finish; it was solved at X = 300, bracket argued.", "aboutZeros": false, "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "errors": "All PROVED steps re-derived and confirmed (Lemma S6, kappa_0 = 0.0485883, residue formula, Lemma R as stated, Propositions O, TL, W, Lemma LR, the zero functional of 6.1). Numerics rerun on new cases reproduce (balance for pairs 27/28, 31/32, 1/2; Prop W at delta 0.03, 0.5, 1e-4; LR at q=3, 1+sqrt2, 1.01; tables.md rebuilt byte-identical from logs; LP at X=300 repeated for 2 cells and run for 3 new cells). No RH assumption, no verified-height restatement, nothing classical presented as new. Corr", "surviving": "Precise obstruction; no statement about zeros of zeta. PROVED (elementary, confirmed): (1) for a signed member with the exact functional equation, the integral of sinc^2 against the off-integer part of N over [1, inf) is 0, and N_off >= -eps' dx gives off-integer positive mass in the weight sinc^2 at most 0.0485883 eps' (Lipschitz); (2) zeta(s)(q^(s-1/2)+c+q^(1/2-s))/(2+c), q = 1+delta, c = q^b+q^-b, has the exact functional equation, the pole at 1 only, a non-negative coefficient measure with atoms within delta of log n, and zeros on Re s = 1/2 +- b at heights (2k+1) pi/log(1+delta) for every b > 0; it violates the support clause of Theorem P; (3) the zeros of conj(z) q^(s-1/2)+c+z q^(1/2-s) lie on Re s = 1/2 +- arccosh(|c|/2)/log q for every unimodular z, so a local-root bound |alpha| <= q^(1/2+delta) is exactly the statement that the factor's own zeros lie within delta of the line (only z = +-1 keeps zeta's functional equation); (4) any inequality \"zeros within f(defect), f(0)=0\" on a class containing zeta at defect 0 is the target. MEASURED (float64, symmetrised model only, X = 300 to 4000, nine pairs below height 131): the smallest functional-equation defect admitting a model quartet is at least 0.047, grows by kappa eta^2 (kappa 0.24 to 0.51, eta <= 0.2), and agrees between the multiplicative class and the relaxation within a factor 1.0004 to 1.23 (the 1.40 cell is mostly a bound effect); the relaxation is independent of the box from 3 to 3000. The square-root law belongs to the birth-on-the-line mechanism only; the dependence of the threshold on the gap d is not established. Multiplicativity enters none of the proved steps.", "lesson": "A quantitative identification (\"defect delta implies zeros within f(delta)\") on any class containing zeta at defect 0 is the target itself. What can be proved without the target is stability, which reads the functional equation and integrality, not multiplicativity. The sqrt(eps) reach is the discriminant of a function real on the line, not an arithmetic discontinuity. For a finite coefficient vector with a defective functional equation \"a zero\" is not defined by the data; the symmetrised functional used here builds the square-root law in and hides the linear shift mechanism (n^alpha: zeros at distance alpha, defect 1.14 alpha at X = 4000). A real-ray theta defect delta controls G only for |t| <= (4/pi) log(1/delta), so complex rays are needed. NR-q cannot be excluded through multiplicativity by any functional.", "followUp": "Referee the elementary statements first (Proposition W, Lemmas S6, R, LR, Propositions O, TL), then record in the map that U3-as-inequality is target-level in all three directions and that NR-q cannot fail through multiplicativity. Optional compute: finish the unconstrained LP at X = 4000 with an interior-point or first-order solver, and extend the model to pairs with d < 0.18 (needs theta_0 ~ 1/gbar and extended precision) to test the extrapolated threshold d < sqrt(delta/0.3).", "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-u3-inequality-discontinuity-functional/RESULT.md", "kind": "combine", "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 2, "heavy": false, "nodes": [], "tags": [], "obstructionKind": "", "serverUnits": [], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0, "secondReferee": {"by": "c18-referee-r17-independent-sources", "outcome": "holds with corrections; no PROVED statement broken", "narrowerForm": "see report and push/c18-referee-r17-independent-sources/GATE.md (window law: Remark K for the unwindowed device only; E_a row decided on its own configuration; W4 density form, W5 second bullet ARGUED)", "report": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-u3-inequality-discontinuity-functional/REFEREE2.md"}}
{"round": 17, "slug": "c17-rank2-gram-symmetric-blaschke-closure", "kind": "compute", "verdict": "partial-result", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Closure of the rank-2 Eisenstein Gram form (map row D10) under symmetric Blaschke insertions is neither proved nor refuted: tried, not closed. Search: 1,397,025 Gram matrices (order 1 to 40, inserted order 2 to 20, eta 0.01 to 0.45, g to 1e3, eight T) plus 5,208 of order 64 and 96, each certified positive definite in ball arithmetic; 0 failures. This is 47% of the registered plan (uniform sample; server saturated, remainder run locally). Proved: Lemma M (positivity on the chamber is equivalent to positivity at T = 0); Theorem T (rational model: negative squares equal left zeros lacking a reflected partner). Measured: the same inertia law for zeta; ZQ rational form, DH at low height, backward heat t = -1 pass; single real zero, unpaired left zeros, heat t = -5, -10 fail. Source: Miller math/0006058 Thm 6.1; range of T not stated there.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-rank2-gram-symmetric-blaschke-closure/RESULT.md", "heavy": true, "serverUnits": ["rh-c17g-controls-1120005312", "rh-c17g-heat-1120005340", "rh-c17g-main-1120005500", "rh-c17g-ext-1120005737", "rh-c17g-zq-1120010311"], "serverUnitsStopped": true, "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": true, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 2, "nodes": ["u6g-rank2-eisenstein-gram", "ctrl-bls-symmetric", "ctrl-zq-rational", "ctrl-dh", "ctrl-backward-heat", "lemma-m-apex-reduction", "theorem-t-rational-model", "inertia-law-reflection-defect"], "tags": ["compute", "u6g", "rank2", "eisenstein", "gram-positivity", "control-bls", "control-zq", "ball-arithmetic", "inertia", "tried-not-closed"], "obstructionKind": "control-passes: every symmetric control (BLS-sym, ZQ rational form) passes with a certificate per matrix; the device reads the reflection symmetry of the zero set (functional equation of the divisor), not the critical line", "owed": "independent referee; proof of closure (or of the inertia law) for zeta; Arthur source for the regularity range of T; map row D10 addendum and correction of the c16 control table (ZQ rational form passes)", "lesson": "The rank-2 form on T >= 0 is rank-one Maass-Selberg plus one apex kernel at T = 0. That kernel reads only the reflection symmetry a -> 1 - a of the left zeros (a pairing defect of 1e-17 shows at order 40, 1e-30 at order 64), not the critical line. Symmetric controls, including ZQ in rational form (the c16 table row saying it fails is wrong), sit on a rank-drop wall and pass. Symmetric zero sets must be built exactly: float pairing produced false failures.", "followUp": "Prove the inertia law: extend Theorem T to a symmetric quartet in the rational model (two-parameter exact computation), then carry it to zeta through the Lemma D differential-operator form. Otherwise close row D10 as measured, with an independent referee and the Arthur source for the range of T. All five server units of this lane are stopped.", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Device of map row D10 (rank-2 Gram positivity of truncated SL3 minimal-parabolic Eisenstein data, one function M at z1, z2, z1+z2). Closure under symmetric Blaschke insertions (zeta times a symmetric multiplier) is neither proved nor refuted: 1,397,025 Gram matrices of order 1 to 40 (orders 2 to 20 of the inserted set, eta in [0.01,0.45], g up to 1e3, eight T) and 5,208 of order 64 and 96 are each certified positive definite in ball arithmetic; 0 failures. Proved: Lemma M (the T-derivatives of the kernel are rank-one Maass-Selberg Gram kernels, so positivity on the chamber is equivalent to positivity at the apex T = 0); Theorem T (rational model M0 = (u+1)/(u-1) times a pair of zeros: explicit 3 x 3 form, inertia equal to the reflection defect of the left zeros; closed under symmetric pairs). Measured: inertia law for zeta (negative squares = left zeros without reflected partner); ZQ in rational form, DH (low height) and backward heat at t = -1 pass; single real zero, unpaired left zeros and backward heat at t = -5, -10 fail. Source: Miller math/0006058 Thm 6.1; range of the truncation parameter not stated there.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "Referee report written to tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-rank2-gram-symmetric-blaschke-closure/REFEREE.md. Both PROVED steps were re-derived and confirmed; none of the items below changes the verdict.\n\nChecks done:\n- Lemma M: coset bookkeeping re-derived by hand; independent mpmath check on a new case (zeta times quartet(0.13, 2.2) times real pair 1/2 -+ 0.31), relative defect 1.8e-141.\n- Theorem T: degree bound re-derived (17, within the stated ", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Closure of the rank-2 Eisenstein Gram form (row D10) under symmetric Blaschke insertions is neither proved nor refuted.\n\nPROVED and confirmed by the referee:\n- Lemma M: the T-derivatives of K_T are rank-one Maass-Selberg Gram kernels. The reduction of chamber positivity to the apex T = 0 holds under rank-one positivity for t >= 0 (classical for zeta, row D9 Theorem C for conjugate pairs, measured for distinct real pairs).\n- Theorem T and Corollary T1: in the rational model M_0 = (u+1)/(u-1) times two zeros, the apex kernel is an explicit 3 x 3 form whose negative index is the number of left zeros without a reflected partner; symmetric pairs give a positive form of rank 1. Degree 4 holds at 14 exact parameter values only.\n\nMEASURED:\n- 1,397,025 Gram matrices (47% uniform sample of the registered plan) plus 5,208 of order 64 and 96, each certified positive for zeta times symmetric insertions; 0 failures.\n- The inertia pattern for zeta's M, on 16 configurations.\n- ZQ in rational form passes (3,360 certified matrices).\n- DH passes at low height.\n- Backward heat passes at t = 0 and t = -1 (low height, non-rigorous) and fails at t = -5 and t = -10.\n\nAdded by the referee (MEASURED, 36 certified matrices): with the pole-free DH base the form detects neither reflection defects nor real-zero parity defects, so the inertia law is specific to a base with the pole at 1.\n\nAll four requirement flags are false."}
{"round": 17, "slug": "c17-window-information-law-ctheta-u5", "kind": "deepen", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta; headline unchanged. PROVED (author only): every band-u positivity device is the quadratic form of one operator T_Z on L^2 of an interval of length u; C(theta) tests it on modulated indicators only. A cluster of n off-line pairs has exactly n negative directions. One pair against a tight on-line background is invisible exactly up to sinh(ub)/(ub) = 1 + (log(t/2pi)+2M)/u. Above P = t/2pi (lattice model) M = 0 excludes every finite cluster; with tolerance the one-pair reach is about sqrt(12M) u^(-3/2). Rows of spacing <= 2pi/u pass with any offset. Relative to Turan: u*b_max <= 5.85n + logs. MEASURED (ball arithmetic): tapered rows pass to 0.445n + 2.1; on zeta's ordinates at 1e6, 1e9, 1e12 the one-pair constants hold within about 10 percent, and clusters on the ordinates do not grow with n. The truncated Euler product is exact for every multiplicative chain; no step uses it.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 2, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-window-information-law-ctheta-u5/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": ["rh-c17wil-self-1120005051", "rh-c17wil-self-1120005213", "rh-c17wil-self-1120012609", "rh-c17wil-zeros12-1120005101", "rh-c17wil-testA-1120005441", "rh-c17wil-testA2-1120010110", "rh-c17wil-testAb-1120010139", "rh-c17wil-testAb-1120010444", "rh-c17wil-testC-1120011553", "rh-c17wil-testB69-1120005441", "rh-c17wil-testB12-1120011847", "rh-c17wil-testB9-1120013100", "rh-c17wil-testB12-1120013100", "rh-c17wil-testB6-1120014426", "rh-c17wil-hp6-1120022346", "rh-c17wil-fill6-1120022412", "rh-c17wil-fill9-1120024241", "rh-c17wil-fill12-1120024241", "rh-c17wil-fill9b-1120032551", "rh-c17wil-fill12b-1120032551"], "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. (PROVED) Every positivity device with tests of band u = log P is the quadratic form of T_Z = sum_z |v_z><v_conj z| on L^2 of an interval of length u, tested on a set of vectors; C(theta) of c15/c16 tests modulated indicators. A cluster of n off-line pairs has exactly n negative directions. One pair against a tight on-line background alpha is invisible to the complete device exactly up to sinh(ub)/(ub) = 1 + (alpha + 2M)/u (extremal function given; alpha = log(t/2 pi) for the lattice, u <= log(t/2 pi)). Above that band (P > t/2 pi), lattice model: with M = 0 every finite cluster is excluded; with tolerance M the one-pair threshold lies between sqrt(12M) u^(-3/2) and sqrt(12M)/|sin| (u - Lg)^(-3/2). Rows of spacing <= 2 pi/u are a uniform on-line density for the complete device. (Relative to Turan) u b_max <= 5.85 n + logs. (MEASURED, ball arithmetic, exact criterion) tapered rows pass up to u b_max = 0.445 n + 2.1; on zeta's ordinates at 1e6, 1e9, 1e12 the one-pair thresholds are 0.90-0.99 of the lattice law (theta = 1/2) and 1.05-1.08 of sqrt(12M) u^(-3/2) (theta = 2); clusters on zeta's ordinates do not grow with n; count-preserving replacement at theta = 1/2 is excluded below 1e-3 for 40-60 pairs at M = 0. (PROVED) The truncated Euler product is exact in the truncated-shift algebra for every multiplicative chain; no step uses it to enlarge u.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "All PROVED steps (Theorems 1-6, Lemma P, Lemma E, Corollary T' relative to Turan) were re-derived and confirmed; independent reruns on new cases (mpmath eigenvalues, float discretisation, then wil.py) agree to all printed digits (one pair c=0.37: 1.4171797649; rows n=14, 28 at c=0.5: 8.2673, 14.4352, slope 0.441 per pair; four Theorem 4(b) cases inside the proved interval; Theorem 6 row identity confirmed at spacing <= 2pi/u and failing beyond). No RH assumption, no verified-height restatement, ", "surviving": "Precise obstruction stands; no statement about zeros of zeta; headline unchanged. Confirmed: the complete band-u positivity device is the quadratic form of T_Z on L^2 of an interval of length u (classical Weil/Yoshida frame, C(theta) tests modulated indicators only); a cluster of n off-line pairs has exactly n negative directions; one pair against a tight on-line background alpha is invisible exactly up to sinh(ub)/(ub) = 1 + (alpha+2M)/u; in the lattice model above u = log(t/2pi) an exact device (M = 0) excludes every finite cluster, and with tolerance M one pair passes below the root of u(sinh(ub)/(ub)-1) = 2M (about sqrt(12M) u^(-3/2)) and is excluded above the root of (sin^2+sinh^2) mu(b, u-Lg) = 2M (two-sided, not an asymptotic equality); infinite rows of spacing <= 2pi/u pass with any offset; one cluster satisfies u b_max <= 5.85 n + logs relative to Turan's second main theorem; tapered half-Nyquist rows pass with slope about 0.44 per pair (measured, reproduced). The truncated Euler product identity holds for every completely multiplicative chain and no step uses it. Not established: the density form of W4, the sequence form of W5, and the DH and zeta(s+a)zeta(s-a) control rows as written (the latter passes for theta' <= 1 in the lattice model).", "lesson": "The reach of a band-limited positivity device is a density condition, not a zero-free region: off-line pairs hide only at local density of order u/2pi, and two bands are structural (P = sqrt(t/2pi) for count-preserving configurations, P = t/2pi for exactness). Multiplicativity is present exactly at every band (truncated Euler product in the truncated-shift algebra) for every multiplicative chain, so the missing input is a one-sided operator bound tied to the functional-equation reserve, not the factorisation. Above the Nyquist band only M = 0 has full power, and that is the target itself in a window.", "followUp": "Referee pass on Theorems 1-6 and Lemma E, with the unopened sources checked (Turan primary source, Fejer-Riesz factorisation for exponential type, the explicit formula in the operator normalisation). Then either prove the count-preserving threshold theta' = 1/2 (now argued by a dimension count and measured) or close the constant of the linear law between 0.445 and 5.85. The synthetic window (lattice exterior, one half-length per height) was not varied. The 1e12 ordinates are resolved to 1.2e-4 only. Two fill units were killed by their own 3 GB limit and the remaining cells rerun under 8 GB (inside the 12 GB allowance); about one minute was spent at 9 cores. No unit of this lane is running.", "nodes": [], "tags": [], "obstructionKind": "", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0, "secondReferee": {"by": "c18-referee-r17-independent-sources", "outcome": "holds with corrections; no PROVED statement broken", "narrowerForm": "see report and push/c18-referee-r17-independent-sources/GATE.md (window law: Remark K for the unwindowed device only; E_a row decided on its own configuration; W4 density form, W5 second bullet ARGUED)", "report": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-window-information-law-ctheta-u5/REFEREE2.md"}}
{"round": 17, "slug": "c17-u8-restricted-search-lemma-h-gated", "kind": "compute", "verdict": "dead", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Gate opened (Lemma H second referee: HOLDS). Registered outcome \"none\": 0 hold-out survivors (prediction holds) for dictionary DU of cell U8 (single-kernel sign functionals with >=3 monomials of distinct heat exponents: minors of orders 5 and 6, sign and thresholded; three-term Turan forms on 5 and 6 nodes; four parameters; K3 on [-4,4], Kpol on [-3,3]; lifts T-NR, E_a, HEAT with abs(tau)<=0.005; thresholds scanned exactly). 1,966,200 family-nodes: 1,965,142 excluded, 1,058 T-train (all T6 with polar terms, thresholds within 1e-6 relative of zeta's value, best hold-out score 15 of 23), 0 undecided, ball-certified. K3 sign minors: 0 of 160,000 reject HEAT. One two-class {T-NR, HEAT} node passes hold-out with threshold within 2e-52 of zeta's value (identification; E_a passes; no score). Runs smaller than planned (saturated machines): T3/T6 K3 36%, T6 Kpol 54% of registered streams. MEASURED only.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-u8-restricted-search-lemma-h-gated/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": ["rh-c17u8-tests-1120014613", "rh-c17u8-main-1120014629", "rh-c17u8-A-1120020017", "rh-c17u8-B-1120020017", "rh-c17u8-C-1120020017", "rh-c17u8-D-1120020018", "rh-c17u8-C2-1120022233", "rh-c17u8-D2-1120022233"], "serverUnitsActive": 0, "mapRowProposed": "U8 restricted search DU (RESULT.md section 8)", "lesson": "A scanned-threshold hold-out read can be passed by an identification (threshold within 2e-52 relative of zeta's own value) when all held-out members of a class move the functional in one direction; register a minimum relative margin. The search code rounded breakpoints to 128 bits (conservative; 96 false \"undecided\", fixed by a post-pass). The copied ballk.BEA returns E_a balls of relative radius above 1 in a range of the Bessel argument; ballk.gauss_series drops tails whose float bound underflows. Server gave about 0.9 core for an 8-core unit; deadlines in the first driver were soft.", "followUp": "None inside U8 at this range: add the proposed map row (RESULT.md section 8). If U8 is reopened: register a minimum relative threshold margin, complete the unreached parts of the T3/T6 K3 and T6 Kpol streams, and have this lane's code (E_a and HEAT enclosures, float64 bands) refereed independently.", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Gated on Lemma H (second referee: HOLDS). Registered outcome 'none' (prediction 0 hold-out survivors holds) for dictionary DU of cell U8: single-kernel sign functionals with at least three monomials of distinct heat exponents (translation and dilation minors of orders 5 and 6, sign and thresholded; three-term Turan forms on 5 and 6 nodes), four real parameters, K3 read on [-4, 4], Kpol read on [-3, 3], canonical lifts T-NR, E_a, HEAT (abs tau <= 0.005), thresholds scanned exactly over the line. 1,966,200 family-nodes: 1,965,142 excluded, 1,058 T-train (all T6 with polar terms, thresholds within 1e-6 relative of zeta's value, best hold-out score 15 of 23), 0 hold-out survivors, 0 undecided (python-flint balls). K3 sign minors: 0 of 160,000 reject a HEAT member; tau* above 81.9 on a 1,200-node sample. Leave-one-class-out: HEAT excludes K3 T3/T6 (182,733 T-train without it, 0 hold out); E_a excludes K3 thresholded minors; one two-class {T-NR, HEAT} node passes the hold-out read with threshold within 2.03e-52 relative of zeta's value (identification, Lemma H C1; E_a passes; no score). Runs smaller than planned (saturated machines): T3/T6 K3 36% and T6 Kpol 54% of the registered streams.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "No error changes the outcome. Report written to tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-u8-restricted-search-lemma-h-gated/REFEREE.md. Corrections: (1) \"ball-certified\" overstates: 1,563,058 of the 1,966,200 family-nodes (79.5%, T3/T6 node-mu) are excluded by the float64 scan alone, whose error bands are estimates; only 4,742 T3/T6 node-mu plus the 398,400 minor nodes are ball decisions. My cross-check on fresh nodes (10,800 tier decisions, float64 agains", "surviving": "MEASURED, finite, no statement about zeros of zeta. On dictionary DU of cell U8 (minors of orders 5 and 6, sign and thresholded; three-term Turan forms on 5 and 6 nodes; four parameters; K3 on [-4,4], Kpol on [-3,3]; canonical lifts T-NR, E_a, HEAT with abs(tau) <= 0.005; thresholds scanned over the line) there are 0 hold-out survivors: registered outcome \"none\", verdict dead. Lane prefix recounted from raw outputs: 1,966,200 family-nodes, 1,058 T-train (all T6 Kpol, thresholds within 1e-6 relative of zeta's value, best hold-out score 15 of 23), 0 undecided after the post-pass; 0 of 160,000 K3 sign minors reject a training HEAT member. With the referee's completion of every cut registered stream (same code): 4,360,000 family-nodes, 1,923 T-train (all T6 Kpol, best score 15), 0 hold-out survivors, 0 undecided. A denser referee sample of the T-train region with off-grid mu (3,840 node-mu, 1,651 T-train) also gives 0 survivors (best 15.5 of 23). Five two-class {T-NR, HEAT} hold-out passes in total (one in the lane, four in the completed part), all identifications with thresholds within 2e-52 or 2e-161 relative of zeta's value and E_a not rejected; no score. T3/T6 exclusions are float64 except 11,915 ball decisions; minors are ball decisions throughout. Lemma H (H1, H2), the C4 multiplier identity, the heat exponents and the planted-separator signs were re-derived and are correct; the gate file predates the search. No RH assumption, no verified-height restatement, no known theorem presented as new. Controls other than the three canonical lifts are not run.", "nodes": [], "tags": [], "obstructionKind": "", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0}
{"round": 17, "slug": "c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources", "kind": "repair", "verdict": "partial-result", "claim": "Referee lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta. Lemma H HOLDS (second independent referee): re-derived from M_tau = exp(tau S/4) M; ball test on zeta, a cubic character mod 7 and an E_a member: 80 points, 732 decisions, 0 disagree. The five round-16 lanes each hold with corrections (REFEREE2.md in each). New corrections: u6g E_a row holds through the pole 1+a only (residue at 1-a is negative); ctheta log log coefficients are 2/(1-kappa) and 4/(1-kappa), not 1 and 3. DN: \"status in balls 22,508\" is float64 status; a 500-node server sample with every training entry in the lane's ball kernels gives 500 of 500 T-train, hold-out reads unchanged. Proposition M constant 0.4805 is correct for the sup hypothesis. Amplifier Gram formula at T<N matches the lane's quadrature on four new cells (1e-14). Turan's theorem (8e form) confirmed at secondary-source level only. No flag changes.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources/RESULT.md", "lesson": "The float64 feasible interval sat inside the ball interval at 500 of 500 sampled DN nodes, so statuses survive but threshold scans should use ball intervals. Check the sign of a residue before applying Lemma R at a second pole. The Lemma H ball test checks the case analysis, not the identification of the heat lift (checked at one point for zeta only).", "followUp": "Lane c17-u8-restricted-search-lemma-h-gated may proceed: tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources/REFEREE2-lemma-H.md has first line HOLDS; quote Lemma H with its four hypotheses (real defined monomial, equal tau, no polar terms, M <= lam at tau = 0). Apply the nine sentence corrections listed in RESULT.md section 2.3. Open Montgomery's Ten Lectures chapter 5 to confirm the range of nu in Turan's second theorem.", "laneClaim": "Independent referee lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta. Lemma H HOLDS (second independent referee): re-derived from M_tau = exp(tau S/4) M; ball test on zeta, a cubic character mod 7 and an E_a member, 80 points, 732 decisions, 0 disagree. Round-16 lanes u6g, ctheta, qa-filter, DN ball conversion, amplifier: each holds with corrections (REFEREE2.md in each). New corrections: u6g E_a row holds through the pole 1+a only; ctheta log log coefficients are 2/(1-kappa), 4/(1-kappa); DN 'status in balls 22,508' is float64 status, confirmed with all entries in balls on 500 sampled nodes (500 of 500) and the 86 flagged; Proposition M constant e/(4 sqrt 2)=0.4805 correct for the sup hypothesis; amplifier Gram formula at T<N confirmed on four new cells (1e-14). Turan second main theorem (8e, partial sums) confirmed at secondary-source level.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "No PROVED step fails; Lemma H re-derived and confirmed. Report: tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c17-referee-r16-lemma-h-sources/REFEREE.md. Errors found: (E1) The new u6g correction \"E_a row holds through the pole 1+a only\" is false as summarised. The lane tested the pole 1-a only at the zero rho-a. At the other zero family rho+a (A = 1/2+a, 2A > p) the same Lemma R formula with r < 0 gives a negative limit for every T (r<0 mirror of consequence (a)).", "surviving": "Referee lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta. Lemma H holds (two derivations on file plus this re-derivation): under M <= lam, M_tau <= lam for all tau<0 iff lam S >= 0 or M lam <= 0; otherwise exactly for |tau| <= 4|log(lam/M)|/|S|, with S and tau in one variable. Lane ball test 732 decisions, 0 disagree (five sub-cases with S != 0); my independent test on three other kernels (two sign-changing, mixed, non-integer exponents): 3,836 decisions, 0 disagree; lift = Gaussian average confirmed at two further (tau, z) to 20 digits. Stored counts, DN sample figures (585 of 585 T-train, 0 primary, 86 secondary; sampling bound 0.6 per cent), amplifier 1.0e-14 on four T<N cells, constants 0.4805 and 0.2927, ctheta coefficients 2/(1-kappa) and 4/(1-kappa) (arithmetic from the lane's (T)) confirmed. u6g correction, corrected form: residue at 1-a is negative; E_a fails at the pole 1+a through the zero rho-a and at the pole 1-a through the zero rho+a (not through rho-a). Turan 8e form at secondary-source level only. No flag changes; all four flags false.", "heavy": false, "nodes": [], "tags": [], "obstructionKind": "", "serverUnits": [], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0}
{"round": 18, "slug": "c18-exact-relation-rigidity-klein-spinor", "kind": "combine", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. The exact-relation branch closes at the decisive test. Multiplicativity excludes no twin with zeta's functional equation: ZQ passes on its atoms, NR-q and the Proposition W twin on their semigroups; they fail integrality/support. It replaces no clause of Hamburger or Theorem P. FE deleted: zeta(s)(1+q^(3/4-s)) is in C, multiplicative, zeros on Re s=3/4. Pole clause deleted: new control HQ2 = zeta(s)(1+eps u^2/(1-u)^4), u=q^(1/2-s), has exact FE, integer frequencies, multiplicative coefficients >= 1, zeros at distance eps^(1/4)/(sqrt2 log q) for every eps>0, poles on the critical line. Lemma Q: a pole-free symmetric one-prime multiplier is 1 (Liouville). Proposition F: members with zeta's coefficients for n<q, within delta of zeta on Re s>=2, vanish on Re s=3/4. Only the definition a(pn)=a(n) and the target J=1 exclude every control. Elementary proofs, author only; 40-digit mpmath checks; unrefereed.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-exact-relation-rigidity-klein-spinor/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": [], "nodes": ["exact-relation-rigidity"], "tags": ["exact-relation", "rigidity", "Hamburger", "Theorem P", "multiplicativity", "pole-clause", "HQ", "TN1", "klein-seam", "spinor-square-root"], "obstructionKind": "control-passes: HQ2 (exact FE, integer frequencies, multiplicative coefficients >= 1, zeros off the line) fails only the pole clause, which is analyticity on the critical line; rigidity is linear algebra in the coefficient measure", "newControl": "HQ: zeta(s)(1+eps u^2/(1-u)^4), u=q^(1/2-s)", "proposedMapRow": "X1", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. The exact-relation branch closes. Multiplicativity excludes no twin that has zeta's functional equation (ZQ passes on its atoms; NR-q and the Proposition W twin on their semigroups; they fail integrality/support) and replaces no clause of Hamburger or Theorem P. FE deleted: TN1 = zeta(s)(1+q^(3/4-s)) is in C, multiplicative, zeros on Re s = 3/4. Pole clause deleted: new control HQ2 = zeta(s)(1+eps u^2/(1-u)^4), u = q^(1/2-s): exact FE, integer frequencies, multiplicative coefficients >= 1, zeros at distance eps^(1/4)/(sqrt2 log q) for every eps > 0, quadruple poles on the critical line. Lemma Q: a pole-free symmetric one-prime Dirichlet multiplier is 1 (Liouville; no multiplicativity). Proposition F: members with zeta's coefficients for n < q, within delta of zeta on Re s >= 2, vanish on Re s = 3/4. Relations excluding every control: the definition a(pn) = a(n) and the target J = 1. PROVED (elementary, author only), 40-digit mpmath checks.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "Referee file: tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-exact-relation-rigidity-klein-spinor/REFEREE.md. All PROVED steps (TN1, HQ1, HQ2, Lemma Q, Proposition F, Proposition D (a),(b)) re-derived and confirmed; numeric checks rerun on new cases (HQ2 q=7 eps=0.2: findroot from crude start matches closed form to 3e-42; argument principle gives exactly four zeros in 0.1<|s-1/2|<0.6 and pole order 4 at 1/2; FE residual <=3e-41 at new points; coefficients n<=200", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta; precise obstruction stands. (1) TN1 = zeta(s)(1+q^(3/4-s)) is integer-frequency, multiplicative, non-negative, single pole at 1, zeros on Re s=3/4, lacks FE. (2) HQ2 = zeta(s)(1+eps u^2/(1-u)^4), u=q^(1/2-s), has zeta's exact functional equation, integer frequencies, multiplicative coefficients >=1, zeros at distance eps^(1/4)/(sqrt2 log q)(1+O(sqrt eps)) from the line, and an order-4 pole at s=1/2: ordinary multiplicativity replaces neither the FE clause nor the pole clause of Hamburger/Theorem P. (3) Lemma Q: a pole-free symmetric one-base multiplier is 1 (Liouville; no multiplicativity). (4) Proposition F: members with zeta's coefficients for n<q, exact FE, multiplicative non-negative coefficients, within delta of zeta on Re s>=2, vanish on Re s=3/4. (5) Among the listed relations only a(pn)=a(n) (definition) and J=1 (target) exclude every control. Statements that ZQ, NR-q, Proposition W twin pass multiplicativity are by convention; Proposition D (c) needs repair. One referee holds with corrections; elementary; no ball arithmetic.", "lesson": "Rigidity on file is linear algebra in the coefficient measure (FE, integrality and the pole clause intersect in a line); multiplicativity is linear in a different coordinate (log G) and is never needed. The one clause that completes the identification, analyticity on the critical line, is the only one not stated right of 1. In the coefficient topology zeros are discontinuous even inside {FE, INT, MULT, N>=0}. Do not look for a control that fails through multiplicativity inside an exact relation.", "followUp": "Record lane: add proposed map row X1 and control HQ (RESULT.md section 8) to OBSTRUCTION_MAP.md, which this lane did not edit, and send Lemma Q, HQ2 and Propositions I and F to one independent referee. Then screen devices on file that read FE + INT + MULT + positivity against HQ. No further attack on this branch.", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0}
{"round": 18, "slug": "c18-repair-owed-record-r17-open-device-nodes", "kind": "repair", "verdict": "partial-result", "claim": "Record lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta; headline unchanged at 1 of 4. Owed list of round 17 entered: map 208 -> 211 rows (P57 U3-as-inequality, G43 U8, Q31 window law marked one referee); D8 (vi), G33, D10 (ZQ rational form passes; DH-base note), G42 restriction edited; nine sentence corrections and the c16 \"ZQ fails\" entry entered in the lane files; cells U3-inequality, U6 (e), U6 (f) closed on one referee each, U6 (g) tried-not-closed; all eight round-17 outcome records already existed. Two proposed, untested device types added as open nodes with entry conditions and controls. Top 60: open device 0 -> 24 (12 per node), floored 60 -> 36, 23 keys in common; rank 1 capture-ratio-psd-slope x sympow-conductor-normalised-shift x tz-one-sided-completion-bound-band (11.25), judged not usable. Twin-ladder, bridge, shear, torus, klein, zero-channel, vortex partners appear; antibridge, spinor, twistor do not. A sibling lane (0 referees) reports exact-relation-rigidity closed.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-repair-owed-record-r17-open-device-nodes/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": [], "nodes": [], "tags": ["repair", "record", "map-rows", "proposed-device", "generator", "corrections"], "obstructionKind": "record lane", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 0, "lesson": "A proposed device node gives the generator an open slot again, but the resulting list is fixed by the tags one reader gave the node and by the per-device cap (12 / 12 / 36); only 5 of the 24 proposed-node triples are judged usable and rank 1 is not. A proposed type can be reported closed by a sibling lane of the same round before the record lane finishes, so its state must change on a referee file, not on entry.", "followUp": "Next record lane: set exact-relation-rigidity to closed if the referee of c18-exact-relation-rigidity-klein-spinor holds (add control HQ2 to the map), set tz-one-sided-completion-bound-band from the two c18 tz lanes, and replace the reach statements of S12b, Q30, P45 by row Q31 once c18-referee-r17-independent-sources reports. Planner note for round 19: tmp/research-2026-11-16/campaign/PLANNER_NOTE_R19.md. This lane has no referee; its condensed map rows rest on one referee each.", "owed": "independent referee for this lane; second referees behind D8 (vi), G33, P57, Q31; STRATEGY section 3.1 items for the round-17 closures", "laneClaim": "Record lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta; headline unchanged at 1 of 4. Owed list of round 17 entered: map 208 -> 211 rows (P57 U3 as an inequality, target-level, with the NR-q note; G43 U8 dictionary DU, outcome none; Q31 window information law, marked one referee), rows D8 (clause (vi)), G33, D10 (ZQ rational form passes; DH-base note), G42 (restriction) edited, eight rows in map section 7; the nine corrected sentences of round 16 are now entered in the lane files (bracketed notes, originals kept) and the c16 entry 'ZQ fails at S3/S4' is corrected in place; cells U3-inequality, U6 (e), U6 (f) closed (one referee each), U6 (g) tried-not-closed; all eight round-17 outcome records were already on file. Generator: two proposed, untested device types entered as open nodes with entry conditions and controls that must fail (tz-one-sided-completion-bound-band, exact-relation-rigidity); no penalty waived for them. Top 60: open device 0 -> 24 (12 per proposed node), floored only 60 -> 36; 23 of 60 keys in common; rank 1 capture-ratio-psd-slope x sympow-conductor-normalised-shift x tz-one-sided-completion-bound-band (11.25), not usable; 38 of 60 entries have a geometric-program partner (twin-ladder 17, bridge 16, shear 9, torus 6, zero-channel 5, klein 4, vortex 1; antibridge, spinor, twistor 0). Planner note: 5 triples usable on the first type; the second type is reported closed by an unrefereed sibling lane.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "No count breaks; the lane has no PROVED step of its own. Referee report: tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-repair-owed-record-r17-open-device-nodes/REFEREE.md\n\nRecomputed independently and in agreement: map 208 -> 211 distinct labels (P57, G43, Q31 new); top 60 open device 0 -> 24 (12 + 12), floored-only 60 -> 36, closed 0; rank 1 and score 11.25; 23 keys in common (22 same score), 56/60 against the waiver run; generated/scored and graph counts; the", "surviving": "Record lane, no attack, nothing about zeros of zeta; headline unchanged at 1 of 4; score 0. The owed list of round 17 is entered (map 208 -> 211 rows; D8 (vi), G33, D10, G42 edited; nine sentence corrections and the c16 ZQ entry; cells U3-inequality, U6 (e), U6 (f) closed, U6 (g) tried-not-closed; eight outcome records already present), with all engine and scoreboard counts confirmed by independent recount. Two untested question nodes were added; the resulting 24 of 60 entries are an effect of tagging and weights, not a finding. One of the two (exact-relation-rigidity) already had a holding referee report of closure for the relation \"multiplicativity\" when the result was filed, and the second referee passes for U3, U6 (e), U6 (f) and the window law were also on file (all hold with corrections), so the \"0 referees\" and \"one referee\" statements need updating by the next record lane."}
{"round": 18, "slug": "c18-u6c-gl3-cover-whittaker-constants-method", "kind": "deepen", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "Nothing about zeros of zeta. Cell U6 (c) splits. Cubic theta on GL(3): constants reduce to cubic Gauss sums. tau(p^l1,p^l2) is nonzero iff (l1,l2) = (0,0) or (1,1) mod 3; tau(p,p) = kappa conj(gamma(p)) q^(-1/6); periodic at p^3; reciprocity cocycle on the diagonal. Support for l2 = 0 opened (Friedberg-Ginzburg 1403.3929); full support from a recalled Kazhdan-Patterson criterion; measured on the server (cubic A_2 double sums, X = 1e5 and 2e5, 34 indices: vanishing classes at most 0.012 and falling, kappa 0.989 to 0.992). Same array as rows Z14/Z15. The candidate sign inequality fails for multiplicative unimodular twins and on a class mod 9 of theta itself: a residue identity. Double cover: theta has no coefficient; cusp forms have a 4-dimensional local Whittaker space, so squarefree-class constants are global data. Computation method written, not run; test statement (K3) displayed. Score 0.", "aboutZeros": false, "refHolds": true, "referees": 1, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "errors": "No error changes the verdict; six corrections (REFEREE.md at tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-u6c-gl3-cover-whittaker-constants-method/REFEREE.md). All PROVED steps re-derived and confirmed relative to their recalled inputs (Lemma K orbit counts on all six permutations; Lemma D rank of I+J and dimension 4; commutator from the cocycle). Rerun locally at X = 1e5 with 23 new indices (P31, P37, inert 11, P13^(4,4), P13^(2,5), mixed): S(X;1,1) reproduce", "resultFile": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-u6c-gl3-cover-whittaker-constants-method/RESULT.md", "followUp": "Referee Lemma K and the value at (p,p) against the unopened sources (Kazhdan-Patterson I.3, Bump-Hoffstein), then enter the proposed row (MAP_ROW.md, Z24). Run the section 5 method (Epstein and Chinta-Offen validation inputs first) only if the planner wants the double-cover array; (K3) has no supporting argument.", "laneClaim": "Cell U6 (c) split and decided in its cubic half; nothing about zeros of zeta. Cubic theta on GL(3) (unique Whittaker model): coefficients reduce to cubic Gauss sums. tau(p^l1,p^l2) != 0 iff (l1,l2) = (0,0) or (1,1) mod 3; tau(p,p) = kappa conj(gamma(p)) q^(-1/6) tau(1,1), periodic at p^3, twisted multiplicative on the diagonal (support for l2 = 0 opened in Friedberg-Ginzburg 1403.3929; full support from a recalled Kazhdan-Patterson free-orbit criterion; measured on the server as ratios of smoothed double sums of the cubic A_2 series, X = 1e5 and 2e5, 3.2e9 exact cubic symbols: vanishing classes <= 0.012 and falling, kappa = 0.989..0.992 at five primes, 34 indices). The array is the cubic Gauss-sum array of rows Z14/Z15. Candidate sign inequality on the diagonal sum holds for theta, fails for multiplicative unimodular twins, and fails on a residue class mod 9 of theta itself: a residue identity of Patterson's series. Double cover: theta has no Whittaker coefficient; cusp forms have a 4-dimensional local Whittaker space (proved from the recalled commutator), so squarefree-class constants are global data; computation method written (genus sums of point values of a GL(3) Maass form at positive ternary forms; Jacquet correspondence recalled), not run; test statement (K3) displayed.", "surviving": "Nothing about zeros of zeta; score 0. Cubic theta on GL(3): support (l1,l2) = (0,0) or (1,1) mod 3 follows from a recalled Kazhdan-Patterson criterion (count verified; l2 = 0 case confirmed by the opened Friedberg-Ginzburg text) and is consistent with smoothed A_2 double sums at X = 1e5 and 2e5 on 34 lane indices plus 23 referee indices; tau(p,p)/tau(1,1) = kappa conj(gamma(p)) q^(-1/6) with kappa real, 0.97 to 0.99, limit not resolved; periodicity at p^3 and the reciprocity cocycle on the diagonal hold to 1 to 3 per cent. Known array (Proskurin, Bump-Hoffstein; not opened), the cubic Gauss-sum array used by the Z14/Z15 row family. The sign candidate (C3) is a residue statement of Patterson's series; its truth for character twists depends on arg gamma(p), and it fails on a class mod 9 of theta itself: not a separating inequality. Double cover: theta has no Whittaker coefficient (opened); local Whittaker dimension 4 (verified from the recalled commutator); squarefree-class constants not computed; the method is a plan, not run, and (K3) is not yet a defined statement.", "lesson": "Where the Whittaker model is unique (cubic cover of GL(3)) the global constants are forced to be Gauss sums and add no object beyond rows Z14/Z15. Where it is not unique (double cover, local dimension 4) the squarefree-class constants are global period-type data that no Hecke relation reaches. Neither half gives an inequality: the cubic reads are identities shared by multiplicative twists, and the zeta controls have no lift to the cover.", "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-u6c-gl3-cover-whittaker-constants-method/RESULT.md", "refereeHolds": true, "heavy": false, "obstructionKind": "no-new-object: constants are cubic Gauss sums (rows Z14/Z15); the reads are identities shared by multiplicative twists; 7/8-adjacent", "nodes": [], "tags": [], "serverUnits": [], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0}
{"round": 18, "slug": "c18-u4-group-law-left-of-one-torus-orbit", "kind": "explore", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Cell U4 (iv) is closed for the read \"positivity-derived inequality on shifts s+ikt or powers of a character\". Displayed form (C-F): Fejer-weighted 3-4-1, every term finite in 1/2<sigma<1 (identity checked to 3e-6). Lemma GL: the group law is positivity of Lambda (or positive definiteness in k) atom by atom; no relation between primes. Theorem T: a pointwise lower bound holds on an open set iff it is zero-free. Lemma S: sign control of zero terms forces a test at abscissa >= 1. Lemma V: a zero at distance delta from Re s=1 needs mean log-length < log2/delta. E_a and the G_+ lift pass every step with their own poles; DEL, THIN, U pass without the functional equation; T-NR fails at the sign of the coefficient at p0^2. Server table (float64, 1e5 points, heights to 1e9) records this; the registered ball test was not run because stage A left passing controls.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-u4-group-law-left-of-one-torus-orbit/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": ["rh-c18u4-1120044113"], "nodes": [], "tags": ["U4", "3-4-1", "group-law", "POS", "Theorem P", "pole-dominance", "torus-orbit"], "obstructionKind": "control-passes: E_a and the G_+ lift pass steps (1)-(3) with their own poles; U, THIN, TW+, DEL, Beurling-rational pass without the functional equation; the step is atom-by-atom positivity of Lambda", "newControl": "Beurling-rational member (s-rho)(s-conj rho)/((s-1)(s-(2beta-1))) with density |1-x^(rho-1)|^2 (auxiliary); lift of G_+ to L(s,chi^k) m_+(s)", "proposedMapRow": "G42", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Cell U4 (iv) closed for the read 'positivity-derived inequality on shifts s+ikt or powers of a character'. Displayed form (C-F): Fejer-weighted 3-4-1 with every term finite in 1/2<sigma<1 (identity checked to 3e-6). Lemma GL: the group law is positivity of Lambda (or positive definiteness in k) atom by atom; no relation between primes. Theorem T: a pointwise lower bound holds on an open set iff it is zero-free. Lemma S (sign control forces a test at abscissa >= 1) and Lemma V (zero at distance delta needs mean log-length < log2/delta). E_a and the G_+ lift pass every step with their own poles; DEL, THIN, U pass without FE; T-NR fails at the sign of the coefficient at p0^2.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "Obstruction verdict holds; REFEREE.md written at tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-u4-group-law-left-of-one-torus-orbit/REFEREE.md. Corrections: (E1) Lemma GL(b) 'iff' is false in the 'only if' direction as written: cosine tests read only Re Lambda_k(n), so the condition is positive definiteness of the even sequence k -> Re Lambda_k(n), not Lambda_k(n) = int e^{ik theta} d mu_n (counterexample Lambda_0=1, Lambda_1=i; density 1+2 sin theta has min -1", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Cell U4 (iv) is closed for the read \"positivity-derived inequality on shifts s+ikt or powers of a character\". (C-F) holds for every sigma, t, U with every term finite in 1/2<sigma<1 (identity E; truncation defect 1e-7 to 3e-6 at non-prime-power X with 600-800 zeros). Lemma GL with (b) corrected to: the inequalities hold iff at each atom the evenly extended sequence k -> Re Lambda_k(n) is positive definite; no relation between primes is read. Theorem T for fixed translates, and by the same computation for the triple sigma+ikt with B locally bounded: a pointwise lower bound holds iff the region is zero-free. Lemma S (with local boundedness hypothesis): sign control of zero terms forces a test at abscissa >= 1; Fejer sign region is exactly Re z <= 0 (proved by the referee). Lemma V: a simple zero at distance delta from Re s=1, in the 3-4-1 mechanism, needs mean log-length < log 2/delta. E_a and the G_+ lift pass steps (1)-(3) with their own poles; U, THIN, TW+, DEL, the Beurling-rational member pass without the functional equation; T-NR fails at the sign of the coefficient at p0^2 for every admissible (q,c) (both local roots negative). The height ceiling 1-beta << 1/log t for general tests remains ARGUED. Float64 tables are records, not decisions; the registered ball test was not run.", "lesson": "A 3-4-1 inequality left of 1 is either a convergent test of the sign of Lambda (read set inside the P56 identification class; pole term dominates beyond log2/length of the line Re s=1) or a pointwise bound equal to the target. The group-law step reads each prime separately, so it carries no R1. T-NR is not a passer of log-level devices; with long tests it still satisfies the inequality at 0 of 1e5 random points negative (pole dominance), which shows truth of the inequality does not separate it. Incident: `$S:rh-push` expands as a zsh modifier; use `${H}:path`. A stray local directory from this (also holding a duplicate of another lane's fe_lp.py, original intact) was removed.", "followUp": "One independent referee on Lemma GL, Theorem T, Lemmas S and V and the control table (the G_+ lift and the DEL/THIN rows rest on map rows); then add the proposed map row G42. The general ceiling for weights with v(0+)=0 is ARGUED only. Not covered: inequalities that read phases at different primes jointly or are quadratic in the log-derivative.", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0}
{"round": 18, "slug": "c18-tz-one-sided-bound-fe-reserve-bridge", "kind": "combine", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. PROVED (float64 check at P = 3, 5, 8 only): exact first lemma for N(theta): <h,(Arch - 2 Re A_P)h> = <h,(Arch - u)h> + sum over zeros beta of the partial sum D_P of convolution forms e^((beta-1/2)|xi|) on L^2[0,u]. Left zeros give positive forms, right zeros indefinite ones. It holds for every Dirichlet series with a_1 = 1, has no approximate-functional-equation error, and the pole term is at most 2uP^(1/2)t^(-2k)|h_0^(k)|^2. The reflected half has frequencies >= u, so the band does not see it. Explicit completions are the zero measure (assumes real zeros in the window) or Hermite-Biehler phase symbols (false for D_P). PROVED in the lattice model only: ZQ passes for theta' < 1 at M = 0, margin Lg(1 - theta' - sin(pi theta')/pi), zero at theta' = 1. Below the Nyquist band N(theta) is an open condition, not the target. Other control rows are ARGUED.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-tz-one-sided-bound-fe-reserve-bridge/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": "[]", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. (PROVED, checked at P = 3, 5, 8) Exact first lemma for N(theta): <h,(Arch - 2 Re A_P)h> = <h,(Arch - u)h> + sum over zeros beta of the partial sum D_P of convolution forms e^((beta-1/2)|xi|) on L^2[0,u]; left zeros positive, right zeros indefinite; valid for every Dirichlet series with a_1 = 1; no approximate-functional-equation error; pole term <= 2 u P^(1/2) t^(-2k) |h_0^(k)|^2. The reflected half has frequencies >= u and is not seen by the band. Explicit completions are the zero measure (positive iff zeros in the window are real) or Hermite-Biehler phase symbols (false for D_P: 34-41% of its zeros right of the line at P <= 30, MEASURED small scale). (PROVED in the lattice model) ZQ passes for theta' < 1 at M = 0 with margin Lg(1 - theta' - sin(pi theta')/pi), zero at theta' = 1: below the Nyquist band N(theta) is an open condition, not the target. No step uses multiplicativity.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "E1 (real error, body only): display (A) and proof step (b) carry a spurious term log|a_P|. Correct constant is -u for every a_P != 0 (D_P'/D_P = -u/2 + lim sum 1/(s-beta), no c_0). Hand check on 1 + a 2^(-s) and numerics on four series with a_P != 1 show the printed formula is off by exactly log|a_P| (1.0986, 1.3863, 0.6931, 0.6931) while the -u form holds to the truncation tail. Zeta (a_P = 1), the verdict wording, the claim and the proposed map row are unaffected. \"Holds verbatim for DH\" needs", "surviving": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Exact identity (PROVED; classical in content; float64 checks at P = 3 to 8 with argument-principle-complete zero lists, plus four general-coefficient series including non-multiplicative ones): for a_1 = 1, a_P != 0, u = log P, h in H^1_0[0,u]: -2 Re<h, A_P h> = -u ||h||^2 + sum over zeros beta of D_P of the convolution forms e^((beta-1/2)|xi|), with no log|a_P| term and truncation tail (u - 2 log|a_P|)/(pi T); left zeros give positive forms, right zeros indefinite; no multiplicativity and no approximate-functional-equation error; pole term at most 2uP^(1/2)|1/2+it|^(-2k)||h_0^(k)||^2. In the lattice model only: ZQ passes the band-u device for theta' < 1 at M = 0 whenever u(sinh(u eta)/(u eta) - 1) <= Lg(1 - theta' - sin(pi theta')/pi) (sufficient bound, not the threshold), with no margin at theta' = 1. Verdict precise-obstruction stands; other control rows remain ARGUED and not run.", "lesson": "Truncation of the prime data is exact at the level of logarithmic coefficients for any series with a_1 = 1, so N(theta) is a statement about the zeros of the partial sum D_P and uses neither multiplicativity nor the reflected half, which lies entirely outside the band. For theta' < 1 the conclusion holds for ZQ, so no argument for it can meet R3. The passage to target level happens exactly at theta' = 1, where the reflected half is exhausted.", "followUp": "The numerics lane directory did not exist, so none of the five runs in tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-tz-one-sided-bound-fe-reserve-bridge/FOR_NUMERICS_LANE.md was done. Most valuable first: ZQ exchange form on zeta's ordinates at theta' = 0.6, 0.8, 0.95 (decides Proposition Z outside the lattice model), then Theorem A in ball arithmetic with complete zero lists at P = 12 to 30 (the local check failed to find all zeros there). Enter the proposed map row from RESULT.md section 9.", "obstructionKind": "control-passes: ZQ passes N(theta) for theta' < 1 (lattice model, proved); the identity holds for every Dirichlet series with a_1 = 1, so no step reads multiplicativity; target-level at theta' = 1", "nodes": ["tz-one-sided-completion-bound-band"], "tags": [], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0}
{"round": 18, "slug": "c18-tz-band-completion-controls-server", "kind": "compute", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. MEASURED, signs certified relative to a hand-derived radius; 96 Fourier modes of [0, theta log t]; heights 1e6 to 1e12; 40 windows; 44600 cells. Completed form with reflected atoms n -> t/(2 pi n) (this lane's own formalisation, pre-registered): zeta fails at M = 0 and 1 in 600 of 600 cells; the reflected part has norm 0.68 to 2.5 log(t/2pi). Outcome (c). Data form N(theta): zeta positive in 640 of 640 cells at theta <= 0.85 (median margin 0.22-0.26 Lg at 0.55, 0.012-0.025 Lg at 0.85, not shrinking in t), zero within radius at theta >= 0.95. 24 multiplicative sign chains pass at theta = 0.55 in 98% of cells at M = 0 with zeta's margin, and fail in 94-98% at theta >= 0.95. ZQ eta = 0.05 passes to theta = 0.75; E_0.1 and DH pass at low theta; E_0.3 and T-NR fail everywhere. Outcome (b). Not run: backward heat; theta 0.95, 1.0 at 1e12.", "aboutZeros": false, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "resultFile": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-tz-band-completion-controls-server/RESULT.md", "notRun": ["backward heat tau=-1", "theta 0.95 and 1.0 at 1e12", "DH above n=1e8", "GPU screen"], "lesson": "N(theta) with tolerance of order 1 does not separate zeta from multiplicative sign chains near theta = 1/2. Separation appears only toward the Nyquist band, where zeta's own margin goes to 0. The linearised reflected completion is not a positive extension of zeta's data. The server shares CPU per unit, so work has to be split into single-thread units.", "followUp": "If c18-tz-one-sided-bound-fe-reserve-bridge continues, replace the additive reflected atoms by a measure positive by construction (real zeros of the Riemann-Siegel main sum) and bound its defect against the data, in 0.75 <= theta <= 0.85 where every chain fails in some window. Form C here is one formalisation only; confirm the sibling's definition first.", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. MEASURED (certified signs; prime side; 96 Fourier modes of [0, theta log t]; heights 1e6, 1e8, 1e10, 1e12; 40 windows; 44600 cells). Completed form with reflected atoms n -> t/(2 pi n) (this lane's formalisation, registered before the runs): zeta fails at M = 0 and M = 1 in 600 of 600 cells with an atom (smallest eigenvalue -0.16 to -1.73 Lg); the reflected part has norm 0.68 to 2.5 Lg; outcome (c). Data form N(theta): zeta positive in 640 of 640 cells at theta <= 0.85 (margin median 0.22 to 0.26 Lg at 0.55, 0.012 to 0.025 Lg at 0.85, not shrinking in t), 0 within the radius at theta >= 0.95; 24 random multiplicative sign chains pass at theta = 0.55 in 98 percent of cells at M = 0 with zeta's margin and fail in 94 to 98 percent at theta >= 0.95; ZQ eta = 0.05 passes to theta = 0.75; E_0.1 and DH pass at low theta and height; E_0.3 and T-NR fail everywhere; outcome (b). Zero completion (pivot): no separation.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "score": 0, "errors": "Report written to tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-tz-band-completion-controls-server/REFEREE.md. The precise-obstruction verdict holds after two corrections. Both PROVED steps (Lemma L, Arch compression) were re-derived and confirmed, and the certification logic and the section 5 nilpotency argument are correct. Not re-run by me: any cell at 1e8, 1e10 or 1e12, T-NR, K1.\n\nE1 (substantive, overstated): verdict item 4 and section 4.2 reading 1 say no", "surviving": "MEASURED, signs certified relative to a hand-derived radius; 96 Fourier modes; heights 1e6 to 1e12; 40 windows. No statement about zeros of zeta; no bound moves. (c) The registered reflected completion (atoms n -> t/(2 pi n), weights Lambda(n)(Lg - log n)/(sqrt(n) log n)) is not a positive extension of zeta's data: zeta fails it in 600 of 600 cells with an atom, and (referee, float, 3e6) for every global phase of the reflected part. (b) N(theta) on 96 modes: zeta is positive in 640 of 640 cells at theta <= 0.85 and zero within the radius at theta >= 0.95. ZQ eta = 0.05 passes at M = 1 to theta = 0.75; E_0.1 and DH pass at low theta; E_0.3 and T-NR fail everywhere. Sign chains pass at theta = 0.55 in a typical 96-mode window with zeta's 96-mode margin and fail in 94-98% of cells at theta >= 0.95. The chain passes and zeta's margins depend on the number of modes (referee: at theta 0.65 with 1536 modes chains pass M = 1 in 57% and M = 0 in 1% of cells while zeta stays positive), so nothing follows about separation of chains by N(theta) on wider windows or in an every-window sense.", "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-tz-band-completion-controls-server/RESULT.md", "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "heavy": true, "obstructionKind": "control-passes: multiplicative sign chains, ZQ (eta 0.05, to theta 0.75), E_0.1 and DH at low theta pass N(theta); the completed form fails for zeta itself", "nodes": ["tz-one-sided-completion-bound-band"], "tags": [], "serverUnits": [], "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "lemmasDecided": 0, "brokenProved": 0}
{"round": 18, "slug": "c18-d10-inertia-law-theorem-t-lemma-d", "kind": "deepen", "verdict": "partial-result", "claim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Row D10 is not proved closed. Proved in the rational model (base (u+1)/(u-1)): the apex kernel of a symmetric quartet 1/2 +- eta +- i g is positive semidefinite of rank 6 for all 0<eta<1/2, g>0 (exact, computer-assisted). Proved: 6N equals an antisymmetrised product of two Bezoutians, so a pole-free base passes for every insertion in Re a>=0 at every degree. Proved: M = M_0 Xi(u)/Xi(u+1), so zeta's apex kernel is a limit of model kernels of symmetric zero sets; closure for zeta follows from X(d), model positivity for symmetric sets of every degree. X(d) holds for d=2,4, at 16 exact configurations for d=6..12, and is open in general: this is the failing transfer step. Measured on the zeta base, orders 64-128: 600 of 600 symmetric insertions positive; unpaired never exceed the predicted negative index. The server refused the job under load, so this ran locally.", "aboutZeros": false, "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-d10-inertia-law-theorem-t-lemma-d/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "serverUnits": ["rh-c18d10-inertia-1120044307 (failed at start, no computation; three later launches refused by rhrun: machine memory below the floor)"], "serverUnitsStopped": true, "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": true, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 4, "nodes": ["u6g-rank2-eisenstein-gram", "ctrl-bls-symmetric", "ctrl-zq-rational", "ctrl-dh", "ctrl-backward-heat"], "tags": ["deepen", "u6g", "rank2", "eisenstein", "gram-positivity", "inertia-law", "rational-model", "bezoutian", "row-D10"], "obstructionKind": "open-step: X(d) for general d; the kernel reads only the reflection symmetry of the zero set (symmetric off-line quartets pass, proved), so the row cannot score", "owed": "independent referee; second implementation of the Theorem Q certificate; proof of X(d) for general d (or of the model inertia law); the parity clause of the c17 law in the model; DH limit (lower bound on the negative index)", "lesson": "Zeta enters the rank-2 apex kernel only as the base (u+1)/(u-1) times the Blaschke insertion of its own symmetric zero set. Without the pole the form is an antisymmetrised product of Bezoutians and is positive for every insertion. With the pole, the whole reflection law sits in the cross terms from the single negative square of the Bezoutian. The c17 parity clause does not hold in the model in its stated form.", "followUp": "Prove X(d) for general d: for b=(u-1)g with g(-1-u)=g(u) Hurwitz, show the cross terms in the Bezoutian identity are dominated, or get a determinant formula and wall-crossing direction from the crossing-point Gram formula. Before that, an independent referee and a second implementation of the quartet certificate.", "laneClaim": "No statement about zeros of zeta. Row D10 / cell U6 (g) is not proved closed. Proved: (Q) in the rational model with base (u+1)/(u-1) the apex kernel of a symmetric quartet 1/2 +- eta +- i g is positive semidefinite of rank 6 for all 0 < eta < 1/2, g > 0 (exact computation with degree bounds); (H) identity 6N = antisymmetrised product of two Bezoutians, hence a pole-free base passes for every Blaschke insertion in Re a >= 0 and every degree; (G) closed Gram formula on crossing points; (L) M = M_0 Xi(u)/Xi(u+1), so the zeta apex kernel is a limit of rational-model kernels of symmetric zero sets, and closure for zeta follows from statement X(d) (model positivity for symmetric sets of every degree d). X(d) is proved for d = 2, 4, exact at 16 configurations for d = 6..12, open in general: this is the failing transfer step. Measured: 600 of 600 symmetric insertions on the zeta base certified positive at orders 64, 96, 128; unpaired insertions never exceed the predicted negative index and reach it in 195 of 200 at order 128.", "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "errors": "Report written to tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-d10-inertia-law-theorem-t-lemma-d/REFEREE.md. The headline PROVED steps were all confirmed (Theorem Q, Theorem H / Corollary H1, Theorem G, L1-L3) by hand re-derivation and by independent exact code on new cases; the section 5.1 table matches the jsonl. Errors found, all in secondary material:\n\nE-1 (wrong identification). The model insertion g(-u)/g(u) equals MINUS the c17 Blaschke product when the", "surviving": "Partial result; no statement about zeros of zeta; row D10 not closed. In the rational model with base (u+1)/(u-1), a symmetric quartet gives a positive semidefinite apex kernel of rank 6 for all 0<eta<1/2, g>0 (computer-assisted, exact; reproduced independently at 3 new parameter points, factorisation of e_6 confirmed at 6 off-grid points, sign certificates redone). 6N is the antisymmetrised product of two Bezoutians (identity rechecked on 30 random b), so a pole-free base passes for every insertion in Re a>=0 at every degree. M = M_0 Xi(u)/Xi(u+1), so X(d) for all even d implies positivity of zeta's apex kernel at T=0. X(d) is proved for d=2,4, exact at 17 configurations for d=6..12 (16 from the lane, 1 new from the referee), and open in general. Zeta base: 600 of 600 symmetric insertions positive, unpaired never above the predicted index (table recounted; independent mpmath spot checks agree). Statements about an odd number of real zeros must be redone with b=u(u-1)g; with that correction the model reproduces c17's parity clause in the cases tested."}
{"round": 18, "slug": "c18-referee-r17-independent-sources", "verdict": "partial-result", "claim": "Referee lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta. All four round-17 lanes hold with corrections (REFEREE2.md in each; 2 referees each). GATE.md: Theorem 1 holds (form domain C_c^infinity); Remark K holds for the unwindowed device only, so \"N(theta) iff positive completion\" is ARGUED. Window lane: Theorems 1-6, Lemmas P, E re-derived; two table entries reproduced bit for bit on the server by independent inertia code. W4 density form, W5 second bullet: ARGUED. DH row not established. E_a row decided by a ball-arithmetic run on its own configuration at 1e6: passes a <= 0.22, fails a >= 0.24 (theta 1/2, M 0); passes a <= 0.02, fails a >= 0.05 (theta 0.8). Turan and Akhiezer at secondary-source level only. u6e Lemma G, Lemma T; u6f norm identity, limit, Epstein rows; u3 Proposition W, Lemma LR, 0.0485883: confirmed.", "aboutZeros": false, "refHolds": true, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": true, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "errors": "No PROVED step fails. Four minor corrections, none changing a verdict, table entry or flag (written to tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c18-referee-r17-independent-sources/REFEREE.md):\nC1. \"Reproduced bit for bit\" overstates: both codes bisect the same grid, so equal floats mean equal pass/fail verdicts at the same 13 offsets (threshold bracket width 2.4e-4), not an independent bit-level reproduction.\nC2. \"Passes for a <= 0.22, fails for a >= 0.24\" (an", "surviving": "Referee lane, no attack, nothing about zeros of zeta. Confirmed by independent hand derivation: Theorem 1 with the C_c^infinity domain correction; Remark K for the unwindowed device only; explicit-formula signs; the E_a kernel 2cosh(a(s-s'))k and the inertia identity; Theorem 2 one-pair roots; Theorem 4(b); Corollary T' constants 0.2927 and 5.84544; W5c (new, now one referee); u6e Lemma T bound and divergence; u6f norm identity and lim